E["npc:doctor-gregory-victor"] = {t="npc",n="Doctor Gregory Victor",z="arathi",s="Doctor Gregory Victor is a Forsaken surgeon stationed at the Horde outpost of Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. Renowned as the premier trauma physician within the Horde, he evaluates aspiring medics seeking to master advanced triage and battlefield first aid. His cold, clinical efficiency keeps frontline warriors stitched together amidst bitter regional conflicts.",h="Doctor Gregory Victor is a Forsaken surgeon stationed at the Horde outpost of Hammerfall in the Arathi...",sec={{t="Surgeon of Hammerfall",b="While many view Forsaken apothecaries with suspicion, Doctor Gregory Victor serves the Horde through practical battlefield surgery rather than blighted alchemy. Stationed deep within the contested Arathi Highlands at Hammerfall, he operates on soldiers battered by Syndicate brigands, Boulderfist ogres, and Alliance forces. His station doubles as the primary proving ground for Horde field medics, demanding ruthless efficiency and prioritizing critical patients under intense pressure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Doctor Gregory Victor?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor is a Forsaken physician stationed at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. He is the master trauma surgeon for the Horde, responsible for overseeing triage operations and instructing advanced field medics.",al={"doctor victor","gregory victor","who is gregory victor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Doctor Gregory Victor?",a="He is located inside the stronghold of Hammerfall, situated in northeastern Arathi Highlands.",al={"gregory victor location","where is victor","doctor victor where"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play for the Horde?",a="Doctor Victor tests promising field medics in battlefield triage through rigorous examination, teaching them how to stabilize the dying and craft advanced cloth bandages for frontline combat.",al={"what does gregory victor do","gregory victor first aid","horde trauma doctor"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is his Alliance counterpart?",a="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen, stationed at Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh, oversees advanced trauma and triage training for the Alliance.",al={"alliance equivalent doctor victor","alliance triage doctor"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Doctor Gregory Victor on?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor is loyal to the Horde and the Forsaken. Stationed out at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, he serves as an expert surgeon attending to the faction's wounded and passing on advanced triage knowledge to those willing to learn.",al={"what faction is gregory victor","is doctor victor horde","doctor victor allegiance"},it="side",add="d46fa605"},{q="What does Doctor Gregory Victor want?",a="Doctor Victor is dedicated to field medicine and surgery. He seeks capable battlefield medics who can handle high-pressure triage, testing aspiring healers to ensure they can prioritize treatments and save lives amid the chaos of war.",al={"what does doctor victor want","doctor gregory victor goals","what is victor doing"},it="wants",add="5e053b25"},{q="Why is Doctor Gregory Victor here?",a="Doctor Victor is stationed in Hammerfall to support the Horde's front lines in the contested Arathi Highlands. With constant skirmishes erupting against the Alliance and local threats, an experienced trauma surgeon is essential to keep soldiers alive.",al={"why is gregory victor here","why is doctor victor in hammerfall","reason victor is here"},it="why_here",add="3e1305a9"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Doctor Victor provides crucial battlefield medicine in one of the Horde's most precarious outposts, ensuring warriors on the Arathi front return to fighting shape.",["race:Undead"]="Unlike the Royal Apothecary Society's toxic concoctions, Doctor Victor demonstrates the Forsaken's mastery over conventional mortal anatomy and restorative surgery."},kw={"arathi highlands","doctor gregory victor","first aid","gregory victor","hammerfall","horde trauma","surgeon","triage"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","quest:6623","zone:arathi","npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Doctor Gregory Victor"}}
E["npc:orgrim-doomhammer"] = {t="npc",n="Orgrim Doomhammer",z="arathi",s="Orgrim Doomhammer was the supreme Warchief of the Old Horde throughout the Second War, remembered as one of the greatest orc warriors in history. Though he died liberating the internment camps in the Arathi Highlands, his legacy endures in the capital of Orgrimmar and through Thrall, who inherited his mighty warhammer and black plate armor.",h="Orgrim Doomhammer was the supreme Warchief of the Old Horde throughout the Second War, remembered as one of...",sec={{t="Rise of the Warchief",b="Originally second-in-command to Blackhand of the Blackrock clan, Orgrim refused the demonic blood offered by Gul'dan, though he concealed his doubts beneath fierce loyalty. Near the close of the First War, disgusted by the Shadow Council's treachery and the murder of his childhood friend Durotan, Orgrim slew Blackhand in honorable combat. Assuming the mantle of Warchief, he ruthlessly purged Gul'dan's warlocks and led the Horde across the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War. Though a devastating strategist who pushed human kingdoms to the brink of ruin, he was ultimately defeated and captured outside Blackrock Spire after the betrayal of Gul'dan split his forces.",sp=0},{t="Fall and Legacy",b="Escaping human captivity, Doomhammer lived in hiding until he met Thrall, Durotan's orphaned son. Reinvigorated by the young shaman's vision, Orgrim rallied what was left of the orcish clans to storm the internment camps and break their people free. During a fierce battle at an encampment in the Arathi Highlands, the Warchief was struck down from behind by a lance. As he lay dying, he bestowed his black plate armor, his ancestral weapon—the Doomhammer—and the title of Warchief upon Thrall. In his honor, the liberated outpost was renamed Hammerfall, and the newly founded capital in Durotar was christened Orgrimmar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Orgrim Doomhammer?",a="He was the Chieftain of the Blackrock clan and the Warchief who commanded the Horde during the Second War. After escaping human captivity years later, he fought alongside Thrall to liberate their imprisoned kin until his death in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who is doomhammer","orgrim doomhammer background","who was warchief doomhammer"}},{q="How did Orgrim Doomhammer die?",a="Orgrim was slain during an assault on a human internment camp in the Arathi Highlands, struck from behind by a knight's lance. Thrall took up his mantle, and the site of that victory was named Hammerfall in memory of his sacrifice.",al={"orgrim doomhammer death","how did doomhammer die","who killed doomhammer"}},{q="Why is the Horde capital named Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall named the fortified city in Durotar to honor his mentor and predecessor. Orgrim saw the promise in Thrall and named him the new Warchief, ensuring the Horde would rebuild on honor rather than demonic corruption.",al={"why is it called orgrimmar","orgrimmar namesake","city named after orgrim"}},{q="Did Orgrim drink the demon blood?",a="No. Orgrim held back from the demonic blood while hiding his doubts behind loyalty to Blackhand, which allowed him to retain his clarity and eventually destroy Gul'dan's Shadow Council from within.",al={"did doomhammer drink blood","was orgrim corrupted","orgrim demon blood"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcs revere Orgrim Doomhammer as the liberator who freed their people from lethargy and interned enslavement, choosing honor over demonic subjugation.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the Alliance, Doomhammer remains a grim symbol of the near-destruction of the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War, having butchered countless champions before his defeat at Blackrock Spire."},kw={"blackhand","blackrock","doomhammer","hammerfall","orgrim","orgrimmar","thrall","warchief"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:orgrimmar","zone:arathi","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:old-horde","topic:second-war","topic:first-war","topic:horde"},src={"Orgrim Doomhammer"}}
E["npc:skuerto"] = {t="npc",n="Skuerto",z="arathi",s="Skuerto is a dwarven scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands. Sent there by Archmage Malin alongside Apprentice Kryten, he aids the Alliance in the field, helping secure magical relics on Malin's behalf.",h="Skuerto is a dwarven scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Scout in the Highlands",b="Skuerto, a dwarf of Ironforge, works as a scout in the dangerous Arathi Highlands. Stationed alongside Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe, he works under the direction of Archmage Malin to recover arcane reagents and potent magical artifacts that once belonged to Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane.",sp=0},{t="Pride and Peril",b="Despite the harsh conditions of the Highlands, Skuerto takes considerable pride in his wilderness scouting and reacts poorly to anyone questioning his competence. His work regularly brushes up against regional perils, from the hostile Syndicate and Boulderfist ogres to dangerous ancient entities tied to the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Skuerto stationed in Arathi instead of Ironforge?",a="Archmage Malin sent him. Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten were dispatched to Refuge Pointe to gather reagents and recover the items left behind by Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane, who fled Stromgarde when it fell under siege.",al={"why is skuerto here","skuerto backstory"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Skuerto's mission at Refuge Pointe?",a="Archmage Malin sent Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten to the Arathi Highlands to collect arcane reagents and recover powerful magical artifacts once owned by Malin's former master, Archmage Trelane.",al={"skuerto purpose","what does skuerto do","skuerto malin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are Skuerto's allies in the region?",a="He works directly with Apprentice Kryten, his partner on Archmage Malin's errand, and with the Alliance defenders holding Refuge Pointe.",al={"skuerto friends"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Skuerto?",a="Skuerto is an Ironforge dwarf scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands. Proud of his reconnaissance skills and notably sensitive to criticism, he operates in the field alongside Apprentice Kryten on behalf of the Alliance.",al={"who is skuerto","skuerto identity","who is the dwarf skuerto"},it="identity",add="9a7bedf3"},{q="Whose side is Skuerto on?",a="Skuerto is firmly loyal to the Alliance and Ironforge. Operating out of the Alliance encampment at Refuge Pointe, he works in coordination with Dalaran mages and local Alliance forces against the threats looming over the Arathi Highlands.",al={"skuerto faction","is skuerto alliance","skuerto allegiances"},it="side",add="1cc8a254"},{q="What does Skuerto want?",a="Skuerto wants to fulfill the mission given to him by Archmage Malin: securing magical reagents and reclaiming powerful lost artifacts that once belonged to Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane, all while defending his reputation as a capable scout.",al={"what does skuerto want","skuerto goals","skuerto motives"},it="wants",add="5f13d7e3"},{q="Who is Skuerto tied to?",a="Beyond working under Archmage Malin and alongside Apprentice Kryten, Skuerto stands with the Alliance defenders holding Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"skuerto ties","skuerto connections","who does skuerto know"},it="ties",add="44066d31"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Skuerto exemplifies the grit of dwarves serving on the Alliance's wild frontiers, though his pride as a scout is easily bruised."},kw={"arathi highlands","archmage malin","ironforge","refuge pointe","scout","skuerto","trelane"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","npc:archmage-malin","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},src={"Skuerto"}}
E["quest:635"] = {t="quest",n="Crystal in the Mountains",z="arathi",s="The Pendant of Myzrael pulses in your hand and a pleading reaches you, as if someone desperately needs help. A vision shows a gleaming crystal rising out of the ground in the northern mountains of Arathi, and you feel drawn to that place.",h="The Pendant of Myzrael pulses in your hand and a pleading reaches you, as if someone desperately needs help.",sec={{t="A Silent Plea",b="The pendant pulses as you hold it. From it comes a sense of pleading, as if someone is trying to reach you and badly needs your help. Then a vision opens before you: the mountains in the north of Arathi, and a gleaming crystal thrusting up out of the ground. You feel drawn to that place.",sp=0},{t="At the Crystal",b="When you find the crystal, it pulses, as if a living force were trapped within it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What starts this journey?",a="It begins with the Pendant of Myzrael. When you hold it, it pulses and you feel a pleading from someone who desperately needs your help.",al={"how to get crystal in the mountains","where does pendant of myzrael come from","crystal in the mountains start"}},{q="Where does the vision lead?",a="It leads to a gleaming crystal standing in the northern mountains of Arathi, and you feel drawn to that place.",al={"where is the crystal","crystal in the mountains location","find the crystal from vision"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","crystal","crystal in the mountains","pendant of myzrael","shards of myzrael","vision"},rel={"zone:arathi"},m={start="Pendant of Myzrael",["end"]="Shards of Myzrael",level="35",id=635},src={"Crystal in the Mountains"}}
E["quest:639"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Strom",z="arathi",s="Zengu in Hammerfall wants the sigils that guard Trol'kalar, the sword of Lord Ignaeus Trollbane. The first, the Sigil of Strom, was taken by the Syndicate, and a Syndicate agent in Stromgarde is likely to hold it.",h="Zengu in Hammerfall wants the sigils that guard Trol'kalar, the sword of Lord Ignaeus Trollbane.",sec={{t="The Legacy of Trollbane",b="In ancient times the trolls fought the Arathorian Empire, and their ablest foe was Lord Ignaeus of Strom, called Trollbane. He went into battle wielding Trol'kalar, a name that means troll slayer in the trolls' old tongue. Now Trollbane's sons are weakened and their stronghold lies in ruins.",sp=0},{t="The First Sigil",b="Several sigils protect the sword, and the survivors of Stromgarde each took a share of them. Zengu says they must all be retrieved. The Syndicate seized the first, and Zengu reckons one of their agents in Stromgarde has it. Bring it back to him at Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zengu?",a="Zengu is at Hammerfall, in Arathi. He is gathering the sigils that protect Trol'kalar, the sword of Lord Ignaeus Trollbane.",al={"who gives sigil of strom","zengu hammerfall"}},{q="What is Trol'kalar?",a="Trol'kalar means troll slayer in the trolls' ancient tongue. Lord Ignaeus of Strom, called Trollbane, rode into battle with it against the trolls.",al={"what is trolkalar","trol'kalar meaning","trollbane sword"}},{q="Why is the Sigil of Strom needed?",a="The sword is guarded by several sigils, which the survivors of Stromgarde split up between them. Zengu wants them all, and the Sigil of Strom is the first.",al={"why get the sigil","purpose of sigil of strom"}},{q="Who holds the Sigil of Strom?",a="The Syndicate took it. It is most likely carried by one of their agents in Stromgarde.",al={"who has the sigil of strom","where is the sigil of strom","syndicate sigil"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","ignaeus","sigil of strom","stromgarde","syndicate","trol'kalar","trollbane","zengu"},rel={"quest:638","quest:640","quest:645","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","topic:syndicate","topic:troll"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Zengu",level="37",faction="Horde",id=639},src={"Sigil of Strom (Classic)"}}
E["quest:640"] = {t="quest",n="The Broken Sigil",z="arathi",s="After you took the first sigil from the Syndicate, Zengu sends you after the remaining two, which the dug-in Stromgarde militia guards. Galen, son of Thoras Trollbane, broke the Sigil of Thoradin into pieces, and you are to carry them to the troll shaman Tor'gan in Hammerfall.",h="After you took the first sigil from the Syndicate, Zengu sends you after the remaining two, which the dug-in...",sec={{t="A Sigil in Pieces",b="Three sigils guard the tomb of Thoras Trollbane, and you have already recovered the first from the Syndicate. The other two are harder to get, since the firmly entrenched Stromgarde militia holds them. Thoras' son, Galen, divided the Sigil of Thoradin into eleven pieces and dispersed them among the Stromgarde defenders.",sp=0},{t="To Tor'gan",b="Zengu tells you to retrieve the pieces from the defenders in Stromgarde and take them to Tor'gan, the troll shaman at Hammerfall, who can bind them into the whole sigil.",sp=0},{t="At Hammerfall",b="Tor'gan says Zengu told him you needed his help. Seeing the pieces, he judges the work not too difficult, since all of them are present and the magical structure is easy to reform. He warns you to close your eyes, and soon declares the Sigil of Thoradin whole once again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Sigil of Thoradin?",a="It is one of three sigils protecting Thoras Trollbane's tomb. His son Galen divided it into eleven pieces and dispersed them among the Stromgarde defenders.",al={"sigil of thoradin lore","broken sigil meaning","what is the broken sigil"}},{q="Who divided the sigil?",a="Galen, the son of Thoras Trollbane, divided the Sigil of Thoradin into eleven pieces and dispersed them among the Stromgarde defenders.",al={"who broke the sigil","why is the sigil broken","galen trollbane sigil"}},{q="Where are the sigil fragments held?",a="The pieces are with the defenders in Stromgarde, where the firmly entrenched militia holds the remaining sigils.",al={"where to find fragments","who has the fragments","stromgarde defenders sigil"}},{q="Who can bind the broken sigil?",a="Tor'gan, the troll shaman at Hammerfall, will be able to bind the pieces into the complete sigil.",al={"who fixes the sigil","torgan sigil","who binds the fragments"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows Sigil of Strom, in which you retrieved the first sigil from the Syndicate.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before the broken sigil","sigil chain start"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","broken sigil","galen trollbane","hammerfall","sigil of thoradin","stromgarde","thoras trollbane","tor'gan","zengu"},rel={"quest:641","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:645","topic:shaman","topic:syndicate","topic:troll"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Tor'gan",level="40",faction="Horde",id=640},src={"The Broken Sigil"}}
E["quest:641"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Thoradin",z="arathi",s="Tor'gan's reconstruction of the broken sigil worked flawlessly. The restored Sigil of Thoradin can now open the seal on Trollbane's tomb, and he tells you to return it to Zengu in Hammerfall.",h="Tor'gan's reconstruction of the broken sigil worked flawlessly.",sec={{t="The Restored Sigil",b="Tor'gan says the reconstruction worked flawlessly, and the Sigil of Thoradin is now able to open the seal on Trollbane's tomb. Take it back to Zengu in Hammerfall, who no doubt has more for you to do.",sp=0},{t="Halfway There",b="Zengu asks if you have the second sigil, and then says they are halfway to taking Trol'kalar out of Trollbane's tomb. The third sigil's whereabouts are uncertain, because those who hold it keep moving about Arathi, but he trusts you will find it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Sigil of Thoradin used for?",a="The restored sigil can open the seal on Trollbane's tomb.",al={"sigil of thoradin purpose","what does sigil of thoradin do","why do we need the sigil"}},{q="Who do you bring the Sigil of Thoradin to?",a="Zengu in Hammerfall. Tor'gan, who restored the sigil, tells you to return it to Zengu.",al={"where do i take the sigil","who turns in sigil of thoradin","sigil of thoradin turn in"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the search for Trol'kalar?",a="It follows The Broken Sigil, in which Tor'gan reconstructed the sigil from the pieces you brought him.",al={"sigil chain progress","how far along is this quest","what quest is before this"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","sigil of thoradin","tor'gan","trol'kalar","trollbane's tomb","zengu"},rel={"quest:640","quest:645","quest:638","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi"},m={start="Tor'gan",["end"]="Zengu",level="40",faction="Horde",id=641},src={"Sigil of Thoradin (Classic)"}}
E["quest:643"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Arathor",z="arathi",s="Following the Sigil of Thoradin, Zengu tells you the human prince entrusted another sigil to Lieutenant Valorcall, who commands the cavalry. Find him, and bring the sigil back to Zengu in Hammerfall.",h="Following the Sigil of Thoradin, Zengu tells you the human prince entrusted another sigil to Lieutenant...",sec={{t="The Prince's Cavalry",b="Zengu scoffs that the humans can scarcely call Stromgarde their own, never mind the whole of the Arathi Highlands, yet their prince keeps the last of his horsemen riding about the countryside. Zengu cannot understand why. More important is that one of the sigils rests with Lieutenant Valorcall, who leads those riders. Zengu wants him found and the sigil brought back to Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="On Horseback",b="Zengu warns that Valorcall is hard to run down, as his horse carries him across the land swiftly. Once he is gone, Zengu expects Stromgarde's defenders to feel a heavy blow, and the Horde will be one sigil from taking Trol'kalar for itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Sigil of Arathor?",a="The order comes from Zengu, who waits at Hammerfall.",al={"sigil of arathor quest giver","who gives sigil of arathor","where to get sigil of arathor"}},{q="Who holds the Sigil of Arathor?",a="Lieutenant Valorcall, the leader of the human cavalry, who has been given the sigil by the human prince. Zengu says he rides on horseback and is hard to track.",al={"who has the sigil of arathor","where is valorcall","lieutenant valorcall location"}},{q="Why does Lieutenant Valorcall have the sigil?",a="Zengu says the human prince gave one of the sigils to him. Zengu does not say why.",al={"why does valorcall have the sigil","who gave valorcall the sigil"}},{q="Where does this fit in the Trol'kalar chain?",a="It is the fifth step of the long Trol'kalar chain. It follows the Sigil of Thoradin, and the Sigil of Trollbane comes after.",al={"trolkalar quest chain arathor","what comes before sigil of arathor","what comes after sigil of arathor"}},{q="Where do you bring the sigil once it is found?",a="Back to Zengu in Hammerfall.",al={"where to turn in sigil of arathor","sigil of arathor turn in"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","lieutenant valorcall","sigil of arathor","stromgarde","trol'kalar","valorcall","zengu"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:645","topic:human"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Zengu",level="41",faction="Horde",id=643},src={"Sigil of Arathor (Classic)"}}
E["quest:644"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Trollbane",z="arathi",s="Following the Sigil of Arathor, Zengu sends you to slay Prince Galen Trollbane and take the last sigil, the one that unlocks his father Thoras Trollbane's tomb. The prince keeps it on his own person, far inside Stromgarde.",h="Following the Sigil of Arathor, Zengu sends you to slay Prince Galen Trollbane and take the last sigil, the...",sec={{t="The Last Sigil",b="The last sigil that can open the tomb of Thoras Trollbane is kept by Thoras's son, Prince Galen, in person. He is to be found far inside Stromgarde, in a chapel within the districts the militia holds. Zengu warns that Galen is well guarded and a fine fighter, so this could prove very hard. You are to kill him and carry the sigil to Zengu in Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="Zengu's Verdict",b="Zengu asks whether the line of Ignaeus Trollbane is broken. Once it is, he declares that Trollbane blood will no longer haunt his people, and that every sigil needed to claim Trol'kalar is now in their hands. Before long, he vows, they will strike at the trolls of Zul'Gurub, whom he hates.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to retrieve the Sigil of Trollbane?",a="Zengu, at Hammerfall, is the one who sends you.",al={"sigil of trollbane questgiver","who gives sigil of trollbane","where do i start sigil of trollbane"}},{q="Where is Prince Galen Trollbane located?",a="In a chapel far inside Stromgarde, in the part held by the militia.",al={"prince galen trollbane location","where is galen trollbane","galen trollbane stromgarde"}},{q="Why is the Sigil of Trollbane needed?",a="It is the last sigil Zengu needs to open Thoras Trollbane's tomb, and Thoras's son keeps it himself.",al={"purpose of sigil of trollbane","why get sigil of trollbane"}},{q="What comes after obtaining the Sigil of Trollbane?",a="The chain continues with Trol'kalar.",al={"next quest after sigil of trollbane","what follows sigil of trollbane"}}},kw={"galen trollbane","hammerfall","sigil of arathor","stromgarde","trol'kalar","zengu","zul'gurub"},rel={"quest:645","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:638","subzone:zul-gurub","topic:troll"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Zengu",level="42",faction="Horde",id=644},src={"Sigil of Trollbane (quest)"}}
E["quest:645"] = {t="quest",n="Trol'kalar",z="arathi",s="Following the Sigil of Trollbane, Zengu finds that the four sigils have formed a single one that can break the wardings on Trollbane's tomb. He sends you to Stromgarde to retrieve Trol'kalar from the tomb.",h="Following the Sigil of Trollbane, Zengu finds that the four sigils have formed a single one that can break...",sec={{t="One Sigil from Four",b="Zengu finds that the four sigils have come together and formed one, the Sigil of Ignaeus. He has no doubt it can break the wardings placed on Trollbane's tomb. Trollbane lies entombed in Stromgarde, in the Sanctum that lies behind the chapel, and Zengu sends you there to retrieve Trol'kalar. A fenced path beside the chapel entrance, on its right, descends to the crypt.",sp=0},{t="The Tomb Opens",b="Etchings on the face of the tomb match the sigil's own glowing lines. Line one up with the other, and a flash of light swallows the sigil, freeing the legendary sword Trol'kalar from the stone hands that held it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to retrieve Trol'kalar?",a="Zengu, after the four sigils joined into the Sigil of Ignaeus.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","zengu"}},{q="Where is Trollbane's tomb located?",a="His remains lie in the Sanctum behind Stromgarde's chapel. A fenced path on the right of the chapel entrance leads down to the crypt.",al={"where is the tomb","tomb location","crypt location"}},{q="What happens to the four sigils?",a="They come together to form a single sigil, the Sigil of Ignaeus, which Zengu believes can break the wardings on Trollbane's tomb.",al={"what happened to sigils","sigil of ignaeus"}},{q="What is the previous step in this chain?",a="Sigil of Trollbane, the last of the four sigils, comes before this.",al={"previous quest","prior quest","sigil of trollbane"}}},kw={"crypt","sanctum","sigil of ignaeus","stromgarde","trol'kalar","trollbane","zengu"},rel={"subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep","subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:638"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Trollbane's Tomb",level="42",faction="Horde",id=645},src={"Trol'kalar (Classic)"}}
E["quest:646"] = {t="quest",n="Trol'kalar",z="arathi",s="The long Trol'kalar chain reaches its last step. The light slowly fades, and Trol'kalar, held in a stone sheath, is released. Carry it to Zengu in Hammerfall.",h="The long Trol'kalar chain reaches its last step.",sec={{t="A Sword Set Free",b="At Trollbane's Tomb the light slowly fades, and Trol'kalar, kept in a stone sheath, is released. You take the sheathed sword to Zengu in Hammerfall, in the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="What Zengu Says",b="Zengu tells you that Strom and Arathor's forces preyed on the trolls for generation after generation, and that their greatest weapon is now in his people's hands. The slow advance into the humid forests of Zul'Gurub will no longer be a struggle. He says the Darkspear trolls are in your debt, and that he will see the sword delivered to Nimboya at Grom'gol.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Trol'kalar need to go?",a="To Zengu in Hammerfall, in the Arathi Highlands. The sword reaches you still in its stone sheath.",al={"where do i take trolkalar","trol'kalar delivery","trolkalar hand in"}},{q="Where do I find the sword?",a="At Trollbane's Tomb, where the fading light has released it from its stone sheath.",al={"where is trol'kalar","trolkalar location"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="This is the last step of the long Trol'kalar chain, and it follows the earlier Trol'kalar step.",al={"trol'kalar previous","trolkalar chain"}}},kw={"arathi","hammerfall","nimboya","trol'kalar","trollbane","zengu","zul'gurub"},rel={"quest:645","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:zul-gurub","topic:troll","zone:arathi"},m={start="Trollbane's Tomb",["end"]="Zengu",level="42",faction="Horde",id=646},src={"Trol'kalar (2)"}}
E["quest:651"] = {t="quest",n="Stones of Binding",z="arathi",s="After The Princess Trapped, a voice from the iridescent shards tells of four Stones of Binding spread across Arathi that hold it down under the ground. The strongest, the Stone of Inner Binding, can be unlocked only with keys taken from the other three.",h="After The Princess Trapped, a voice from the iridescent shards tells of four Stones of Binding spread across...",sec={{t="Four Stones",b="The voice tells of four Stones of Binding spread across Arathi, holding it down under the ground. To loosen them, the strongest must be unlocked first: the Stone of Inner Binding, which needs keys gathered from the other three, the Stones of West, East and Outer Binding. The keys are the Burning Key, the Cresting Key and the Thundering Key. Guardians watch over the stones, but someone clever or lucky may find a way to banish them. Once gathered, the keys are carried to the Stone of Inner Binding.",sp=0},{t="At the Inner Stone",b="The stone carries the voice of Myzrael: the Stones of Binding are open, the shackles are loosening and freedom draws closer. Myzrael hails you as a noble rescuer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this step come from?",a="It comes from the iridescent shards, after The Princess Trapped.",al={"stones of binding quest giver","who gives stones of binding","where to start stones of binding"}},{q="What are the four Stones of Binding?",a="The Stone of West Binding, the Stone of East Binding, the Stone of Outer Binding and the Stone of Inner Binding, the strongest.",al={"which stones of binding","arathi binding stones","four stones"}},{q="Which keys are needed to unlock the inner stone?",a="The Burning Key, the Cresting Key and the Thundering Key, gathered from the Stones of West, East and Outer Binding.",al={"binding keys","what keys are needed","keys for stone of inner binding"}},{q="Who guards the binding stones?",a="Guardians watch over the stones, though a clever or lucky adventurer may find a way to banish them.",al={"stone guardians","who guards the stones","binding stone protectors"}},{q="Where must the keys be delivered?",a="To the Stone of Inner Binding, the mightiest of them, which has to be unlocked before the others will open.",al={"where do i take the keys","turn in stones of binding","stone of inner binding location"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","burning key","cresting key","iridescent shards","myzrael","stone of inner binding","stones of binding","thundering key"},rel={"quest:642","quest:652","zone:arathi"},m={start="Iridescent Shards",["end"]="Stone of Inner Binding",level="38",id=651},src={"Classic quest text: Stones of Binding"}}
E["quest:652"] = {t="quest",n="Breaking the Keystone",z="arathi",s="Once the Stones of Binding were opened, much of the voice's confinement eased, yet a lock still holds it. That lock is the Keystone among a ring of stones, and the stone watcher Fozruk, one of the voice's captors, holds the key, known to the watchers as the Rod of Order.",h="Once the Stones of Binding were opened, much of the voice's confinement eased, yet a lock still holds it.",sec={{t="The Last Lock",b="With the Stones of Binding opened, the voice's confinement has eased a great deal, but one lock remains: the Keystone, among the circle of stones around you. Its key is held by a captor, the stone watcher Fozruk, and the watchers call it the Rod of Order. Taking the rod from Fozruk and carrying it to the Keystone is how the lock will open. The voice promises that its gratitude, if you manage this, will shake the earth to its roots. The Keystone itself is charged with immense geomantic energy.",sp=0},{t="At the Keystone",b="When the rod is set into the Keystone, a tremor runs beneath you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What comes before this step?",a="Stones of Binding came first, and opening those stones loosened much of the voice's confinement.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","stones of binding prerequisite"}},{q="Who is Fozruk?",a="Fozruk is a stone watcher and one of the voice's captors, who holds the key to the Keystone.",al={"who is fozruk","fozruk lore","stone watcher fozruk"}},{q="What is the Rod of Order?",a="The name the stone watchers use for the key to the Keystone, which Fozruk holds.",al={"rod of order","what is rod of order","keystone key"}},{q="Where is the Keystone?",a="The Keystone stands among a circle of stones in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where is breaking the keystone","keystone location","stone circle arathi"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","fozruk","keystone","rod of order","stone of inner binding","stone watcher"},rel={"quest:651","zone:arathi"},m={start="Stone of Inner Binding",["end"]="Keystone",level="42",id=652},src={"Classic quest text: Breaking the Keystone"}}
E["quest:653"] = {t="quest",n="Myzrael's Allies",z="arathi",s="Myzrael cries out that she is free, and that she will gather her strength in hiding from her captors. She calls you a noble ally and sends you to Gerrig Bonegrip in a shop of Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, who knows how she can be summoned.",h="Myzrael cries out that she is free, and that she will gather her strength in hiding from her captors.",sec={{t="Free to Gather Strength",b="Myzrael is free, and means to gather strength hidden from her captors, since if they met her now they would surely overpower her and lock her away again. In time she means to face the giants, and she swears they will rue having held her. She calls you a noble ally and says she will need your help again, to summon her to the surface when she is ready.",sp=0},{t="Word for Gerrig Bonegrip",b="Myzrael tells you to speak with Gerrig Bonegrip, whose shop is in Ironforge, in the Forlorn Cavern. He knows how she can be summoned.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Gerrig Bonegrip be found?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip keeps a shop in the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge.",al={"gerrig bonegrip location","where is gerrig bonegrip","find gerrig bonegrip"}},{q="Why is Myzrael remaining in hiding?",a="She needs to gather her strength first. If her captors faced her now, they would surely overpower her and imprison her again.",al={"why is myzrael hiding","where is myzrael going"}},{q="Who are the captors Myzrael speaks of?",a="The giants, who had wardship of her. She says that in time she will confront them and they will regret it.",al={"myzrael captors","who imprisoned myzrael","myzrael giants"}},{q="Why does Myzrael send you to Ironforge?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip knows how she can be summoned, and she says she will need you to summon her to the surface when she is ready.",al={"why go to ironforge","purpose of visiting gerrig"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","giants","ironforge","keystone","myzrael"},rel={"npc:gerrig-bonegrip","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ironforge","zone:arathi"},m={start="Keystone",["end"]="Gerrig Bonegrip",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=653},src={"Myzrael's Allies (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:656"] = {t="quest",n="Summoning the Princess",z="arathi",s="Theldurin the Lost says Myzrael must be beaten while she is still growing, before her strength is enough to challenge those who hold her captive. At the Shards of Myzrael you call her forth, defeat her, and bind her Eldritch Shackles to the Shards.",h="Theldurin the Lost says Myzrael must be beaten while she is still growing, before her strength is enough to...",sec={{t="Why She Must Be Stopped",b="Theldurin wants Myzrael stopped before her power swells enough to set her against her captors. Some claim she can be controlled; Theldurin asks why, then, the giants bothered to chain her at all.",sp=0},{t="At the Shards",b="You take the Scroll of Myzrael to the Shards, the place where you first talked with her, and call her up. After you defeat her, her Eldritch Shackles are yours to bind to the Shards, and she is trapped once more.",sp=0},{t="When the Shackles Are Placed",b="As the shackles settle around the Shards, a wail rises from far below, followed by a roar. The warmth and sense of safety the Shards once gave is gone. Now they pulse with open menace, as though the thing beneath them bears the surface ill will.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to fight Myzrael?",a="Theldurin the Lost, who warns that Myzrael must be beaten before her strength grows enough to challenge her captors.",al={"quest giver","who gives summoning the princess","theldurin quest"}},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="At the Shards of Myzrael, the place where you first talked with her.",al={"where to summon myzrael","shards of myzrael location","summoning spot"}},{q="Why does Theldurin want Myzrael defeated?",a="Theldurin fears she will grow strong enough to challenge her captors. Theldurin also points out that if she could truly be controlled, the giants would not have chained her.",al={"why kill myzrael","theldurin motivation","why summon her"}},{q="How is Myzrael summoned?",a="With the Scroll of Myzrael, used at the Shards of Myzrael.",al={"how to summon her","scroll of myzrael use","summoning process"}},{q="What do you do with the Eldritch Shackles?",a="Defeat Myzrael, take her shackles, and fasten them to the Shards. Then she is trapped again.",al={"what item do i need","eldritch shackles","shackles of myzrael"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","eldritch shackles","myzrael","scroll of myzrael","shards of myzrael","theldurin the lost"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","zone:arathi"},m={start="Theldurin the Lost",["end"]="Shards of Myzrael",level="50",id=656},src={"Summoning the Princess"}}
E["quest:662"] = {t="quest",n="Deep Sea Salvage",z="arathi",s="Following Land Ho!, First Mate Nilzlix asks you to bring back the charts and logs of two sunken ships before anyone leaves the cove.",h="Following Land Ho!, First Mate Nilzlix asks you to bring back the charts and logs of two sunken ships before...",sec={{t="Two Ships Lost in the Reef",b="O'Breen led three ships into the cove, certain the treasure lay here. The Harbinger docked safely. Then, as the Maiden's Folly with the Spirit of Silverpine came in, the tides began to lower, and both ships ran aground on a temple-like structure in the reef and sank fast.",sp=0},{t="What Nilzlix Wants Back",b="Nilzlix wants the logs and the charts of both wrecked ships recovered, since that information must not be left behind for prying eyes. If it reached enemy hands, he says, Fleet Master Seahorn would force the crew down the plank.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine sink?",a="As the two ships came in, the tides began to lower. Both ran aground on something like a temple in the reef and sank quickly.",al={"why did the ships wreck","how did the ships sink","arathi cove shipwreck cause"}},{q="Who is First Mate Nilzlix?",a="He is the first mate who speaks of the three ships O'Breen led into the cove, and he wants the logs and charts of the two sunken ones recovered.",al={"nilzlix","who gives deep sea salvage"}},{q="Why are the charts and logs so important?",a="Nilzlix does not want that information left behind for prying eyes. If enemies got hold of it, he says Fleet Master Seahorn would force the crew down the plank.",al={"why recover logs","why charts and logs"}},{q="What ship made it to safety?",a="Only the Harbinger. It docked safely in the cove, while the other two ships went down.",al={"which ship survived","harbinger ship"}},{q="Who is Fleet Master Seahorn?",a="Nilzlix names him as the one who would force the crew down the plank if their records reached enemy hands.",al={"fleet master seahorn role","who is seahorn"}},{q="What came before this task?",a="It follows Land Ho!",al={"deep sea salvage prerequisite","previous quest"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","booty bay","deep sea salvage","harbinger","maiden's folly","nilzlix","o'breen","seahorn","spirit of silverpine"},rel={"quest:663","npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="First Mate Nilzlix",["end"]="First Mate Nilzlix",level="40",id=662},src={"Deep Sea Salvage"}}
E["quest:663"] = {t="quest",n="Land Ho!",z="arathi",s="At Faldir's Cove, the lookout Lolo greets you with news that Captain O'Breen's stop here will last far longer than planned. Two ships of the formation, the Spirit of Silverpine and the Maiden's Folly, are lost, and Lolo suggests you speak with the captain.",h="At Faldir's Cove, the lookout Lolo greets you with news that Captain O'Breen's stop here will last far longer...",sec={{t="Lolo's Welcome",b="Lolo, ever on the lookout, spots you arriving at Faldir's Cove. Captain O'Breen had promised the crew only a few hours here, time enough to collect the treasure and head back to Booty Bay. Lolo doubts it will be so quick. Two ships of the formation, the Spirit of Silverpine and the Maiden's Folly, now rest on the bottom of the sea. Anyone who means to stay is told to talk to the captain.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Account",b="Captain O'Breen calls the whole affair a horrible mess and fears Seahorn will take the ship if word gets out. One of the Professor's contraptions pointed to the lost treasure near the cove, so the Harbinger came in to dock and the two other ships were signaled to follow. Then the sea rumbled, the water drew back, and both ships crashed into the reef. It is not just a reef, the captain says, and something is down there. Help for the crew is promised a handsome payment.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the other ships?",a="Two ships of the formation, the Spirit of Silverpine and the Maiden's Folly, were lost and lie on the bottom of the sea.",al={"where are the other ships","sunken ships faldir","what sank the ships"}},{q="Why did the crew come to Faldir's Cove?",a="Captain O'Breen came to gather treasure at the cove, expecting to stay only a few hours before heading back to Booty Bay.",al={"why are they here","purpose of expedition","what brought them to arathi"}},{q="Who should you talk to at Faldir's Cove?",a="Lolo the lookout suggests you speak with Captain O'Breen in Faldir's Cove if you plan on sticking around.",al={"who is captain o'breen","where is shakes o'breen"}}},kw={"booty bay","faldir's cove","harbinger","lolo the lookout","maiden's folly","seahorn","shakes o'breen","spirit of silverpine"},rel={"subzone:faldir-s-cove","quest:662","quest:665","quest:664","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="Lolo the Lookout",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="35",id=663},src={"Land Ho!"}}
E["quest:664"] = {t="quest",n="Drowned Sorrows",z="arathi",s="Captain Steelgut sits mourning at Faldir's Cove after losing the beloved Maiden's Folly. Steelgut asks you to go after the Daggerspine naga who slaughtered the survivors of the wreck.",h="Captain Steelgut sits mourning at Faldir's Cove after losing the beloved Maiden's Folly.",sec={{t="A Captain by the Fire",b="Captain Steelgut sits by the fire at Faldir's Cove, wishing for a watery grave instead. The crew fought hard to save the beautiful Maiden's Folly, but the sea sank it, with water rushing in all at once. O'Breen reached shore safely, yet naga killed the survivors. Steelgut wants Daggerspine raiders and sorceresses dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Steelgut?",a="The captain of the Maiden's Folly, now sitting by a fire at Faldir's Cove after the ship was lost.",al={"captain steelgut","steelgut","who is the quest giver"}},{q="What happened to the Maiden's Folly?",a="Steelgut says the sea sank the ship: one second it was afloat and the next water was rushing in, though the crew tried hard to save it.",al={"maidens folly","what happened to the ship","why did steelgut crash"}},{q="Why does Captain Steelgut want the naga killed?",a="Naga killed the survivors of the wreck. Steelgut calls them scum and wants them dead.",al={"why kill naga","steelgut revenge","daggerspine reason"}},{q="Which naga does Steelgut want dead?",a="Ten Daggerspine raiders and three Daggerspine sorceresses.",al={"which naga to kill","target naga","daggerspine targets"}}},kw={"arathi","daggerspine","faldir's cove","maiden's folly","naga","o'breen","raider","sorceress","steelgut"},rel={"subzone:faldir-s-cove","topic:naga","zone:arathi"},m={start="Captain Steelgut",["end"]="Captain Steelgut",level="40",id=664},src={"Drowned Sorrows (Classic)"}}
E["quest:665"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="Now that they are full-fledged Blackwater Raiders, Professor Phizzlethorpe and Doctor Draxlegauge are to help Mr. O'Breen find the lost elven treasure. To search the dark sea for the gems, the professor needs your protection while he charges a pair of goggles at an enchanted stone in a cave.",h="Now that they are full-fledged Blackwater Raiders, Professor Phizzlethorpe and Doctor Draxlegauge are to help...",sec={{t="Charging the Goggles",b="The gems are next to impossible to find in the dark sea without help, so Doctor Draxlegauge has built goggles for the search. They need charging with power from the enchanted stone, in a cave a short way uphill. The cave is cursed, though: those who draw near are ambushed. Professor Phizzlethorpe asks you to defend him while he draws the stone's energy into the goggles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Professor Phizzlethorpe asks you to defend him as he goes to the cave and back, charging the doctor's goggles at the enchanted stone.",al={"who gives this quest","phizzlethorpe","quest giver"}},{q="Why do the goggles need to be charged?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge built them to help find the lost gems in the dark sea. To work, they must first be charged with the stone's power.",al={"why charge goggles","goggles purpose","what are the goggles for"}},{q="Why does the professor need an escort?",a="The cave is cursed, and when they get close they are ambushed. He needs you to defend him while he channels the stone's energy.",al={"why protect phizzlethorpe","what is in the cave"}},{q="Who are the professor and the doctor working for?",a="The professor says they are now full-fledged Blackwater Raiders, so helping Mr. O'Breen find the lost elven treasure falls to them.",al={"who are they helping","mr obreen","blackwater raiders"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","blackwater raiders","draxlegauge","enchanted stone","goggles","o'breen","phizzlethorpe","sunken treasure"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:gnome"},m={start="Professor Phizzlethorpe",["end"]="Doctor Draxlegauge",level="40",id=665},src={"Sunken Treasure (1)"}}
E["quest:666"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="In Faldir's Cove, Doctor Draxlegauge lends you his goggles to find ten elven gems for Captain O'Breen. He expects them back when you finish.",h="In Faldir's Cove, Doctor Draxlegauge lends you his goggles to find ten elven gems for Captain O'Breen.",sec={{t="Gems Turned to Stone",b="The elven gems have lain on the sea floor so long that thick stone has hardened around them. The Goggles of Gem Hunting hold the power to find them through those stony shells. Proud of the gnomish ingenuity behind the goggles, Doctor Draxlegauge lends them to you. The gems are for Captain O'Breen.",sp=0},{t="Dry Land for the Doctor",b="Doctor Draxlegauge says scientific work keeps him on safe, dry land, though he could swim down himself. He expects you to return the goggles afterward. Captain O'Breen, he says, will have plenty of use for them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to gather the gems?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge, waiting in Faldir's Cove, sends you to gather ten elven gems for Captain O'Breen.",al={"who gives sunken treasure 2","quest giver sunken treasure"}},{q="Why are special goggles required for the search?",a="Years on the sea floor have hardened the gems into thick stone. The power in the Goggles of Gem Hunting lets you find them easily.",al={"why goggles of gem hunting","what do the goggles do"}},{q="Why doesn't Doctor Draxlegauge dive for the gems himself?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge says important scientific work keeps him on safe, dry land.",al={"why doesn't draxlegauge swim","why draxlegauge stays on land"}},{q="Can you keep the Goggles of Gem Hunting?",a="No. Doctor Draxlegauge lends you the goggles and expects them back when you finish. Captain O'Breen will use them often.",al={"keep gem hunting goggles","do i return goggles"}},{q="Where does this fall in the Sunken Treasure chain?",a="This follows the first part of Sunken Treasure, when Professor Phizzlethorpe charged the goggles. A third part follows.",al={"what comes before this","what is the next step"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","captain o'breen","doctor draxlegauge","elven gem","faldir's cove","fleet master seahorn","goggles of gem hunting","sunken treasure"},rel={"subzone:faldir-s-cove","zone:arathi","npc:fleet-master-seahorn"},m={start="Doctor Draxlegauge",["end"]="Doctor Draxlegauge",level="40",id=666},src={"Sunken Treasure (2)"}}
E["quest:667"] = {t="quest",n="Death From Below",z="arathi",s="In the Arathi Highlands, Shakes O'Breen expects the Daggerspine naga to attack from the sea, and the crew cannot sail home to Booty Bay without O'Breen's knowledge of the waters. You stay aboard beside O'Breen, man the cannon and drive the naga back.",h="In the Arathi Highlands, Shakes O'Breen expects the Daggerspine naga to attack from the sea, and the crew...",sec={{t="Holding the Deck",b="After Sunken Treasure, Shakes O'Breen sees the Daggerspines gathering to attack. Naga have a name for ruthlessness and will keep coming until O'Breen is dead. O'Breen does not value their own life above those of the crew, but asks you to defend them, since the crew cannot reach Booty Bay without that knowledge of the seas. You wait aboard with O'Breen for the naga to come from the water.",sp=0},{t="Afterward",b="When the attack is over, O'Breen says the ship will leave as soon as the tide rises. O'Breen would have offered you a place on the crew, but sees that you have bigger fish to fry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is attacking Shakes O'Breen?",a="The Daggerspine naga are gathering to attack, and they will keep at it until Shakes O'Breen is dead. They come from the sea.",al={"who attacks shakes","who are the attackers","daggerspine attack"}},{q="Why is protecting Shakes O'Breen so vital to the crew?",a="Shakes O'Breen does not value their own life above those of the crew, but without O'Breen's knowledge of the seas the crew cannot sail back to Booty Bay.",al={"why protect shakes obreen","why is shakes important","shakes obreen navigation"}},{q="How do you repel the naga assault?",a="You remain up on the ship with Shakes O'Breen and man the cannon to drive the naga back as they come from the sea.",al={"how to beat death from below","how to defend shakes","cannon defense"}},{q="Where does this defense take place?",a="On Shakes O'Breen's ship in the Arathi Highlands, with the naga coming from the sea.",al={"where is death from below","death from below location"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","booty bay","daggerspine","naga","shakes o'breen","ship cannon"},rel={"topic:naga","zone:arathi","subzone:booty-bay"},m={start="Shakes O'Breen",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="44",id=667},src={"Death From Below (Classic)"}}
E["quest:668"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="Doctor Draxlegauge hands you the elven gems and sends you to carry them to Captain O'Breen. After a few weeks among pirates, he and the professor know that holding on to their treasure is unhealthy.",h="Doctor Draxlegauge hands you the elven gems and sends you to carry them to Captain O'Breen.",sec={{t="Treasure for the Captain",b="Doctor Draxlegauge does not want Captain O'Breen kept waiting, since the captain will want to see the elven gems for himself. After weeks among these pirates, the doctor and the professor have learned that being caught holding on to pirate treasure is bad for their health. He hands you the gems to carry to O'Breen, who waits at the bridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Captain O'Breen?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge gives you the elven gems and asks you to take them to Captain O'Breen.",al={"who gives sunken treasure 3","draxlegauge quest"}},{q="Why is Doctor Draxlegauge so eager to give up the gems?",a="After a few weeks among these pirates, he and the professor have decided that being caught hanging on to the pirates' treasure would be bad for their health.",al={"why hand over elven gems","why give gems to pirate"}},{q="Where does this fall in the chain?",a="It follows the second part of Sunken Treasure, and a fourth part comes after it.",al={"sunken treasure chain position","what comes before sunken treasure 3"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","captain o'breen","doctor draxlegauge","elven gems","pirates","shakes o'breen","sunken treasure"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:pirate","topic:gnome"},m={start="Doctor Draxlegauge",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="40",id=668},src={"Sunken Treasure (3)"}}
E["quest:669"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="After the previous step in the Sunken Treasure chain, Shakes O'Breen is stuck where he is and needs word taken to Fleet Master Seahorn at Booty Bay. He asks you to carry a sample gem as proof of the find.",h="After the previous step in the Sunken Treasure chain, Shakes O'Breen is stuck where he is and needs word...",sec={{t="Word for Booty Bay",b="Shakes O'Breen wants Fleet Master Seahorn to hear of the find right away, yet he cannot easily get away. The tide is too low, and the creatures they disturbed are watching every move. He asks you to help the Blackwater Raiders by telling Seahorn in Booty Bay that the treasure is found and more is being brought up. A sample elven gem goes with you as proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't Shakes O'Breen deliver the gem himself?",a="The tide is too low for them to get away, and the creatures they disturbed are keeping a close eye on their movements.",al={"why cant shakes leave","why is shakes stuck","why does shakes need a courier"}},{q="Who is Fleet Master Seahorn?",a="He is the Fleet Master in Booty Bay, whom O'Breen wants to hear of the find at once.",al={"who is seahorn","where is fleet master seahorn"}},{q="What proof is being carried to Booty Bay?",a="A sample elven gem, which shows that the treasure was found and that more is being extracted.",al={"what is the proof","what gem is delivered"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","blackwater raiders","booty bay","fleet master seahorn","sample elven gem","shakes o'breen","sunken treasure"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="Shakes O'Breen",["end"]="Fleet Master Seahorn",level="40",id=669},src={"Sunken Treasure (4)"}}
E["quest:670"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="Fleet Master Seahorn, whose ships cannot sail from Booty Bay until they restock, asks you to carry a secret letter to Shakes O'Breen, busy off the Arathi coast.",h="Fleet Master Seahorn, whose ships cannot sail from Booty Bay until they restock, asks you to carry a secret...",sec={{t="A Letter for O'Breen",b="Fleet Master Seahorn sizes you up as the adventurous sort. His ships cannot leave Booty Bay until they have restocked, and he says heavy things are brewing both here and abroad. He needs top secret correspondence carried to Shakes O'Breen off the Arathi coast, and he asks whether he can trust you to deliver the message safely and in confidence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to deliver this letter?",a="Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay gives you a sealed letter for Shakes O'Breen.",al={"who gives sunken treasure 5","who starts this quest","seahorns letter questgiver"}},{q="Why doesn't Fleet Master Seahorn deliver the letter himself?",a="His ships cannot sail from Booty Bay until they have restocked.",al={"why can't seahorn leave booty bay","why is fleet master seahorn stuck"}},{q="Where is Shakes O'Breen located?",a="Off the coast of the Arathi Highlands, where Seahorn says he is busy.",al={"where to find shakes obreen","shakes obreen location","where is shakes"}},{q="What came before this delivery?",a="It follows the fourth part of Sunken Treasure.",al={"sunken treasure chain","what quest comes before sunken treasure 5"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","blackwater raiders","booty bay","fleet master seahorn","seahorn's sealed letter","shakes o'breen","sunken treasure"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="Fleet Master Seahorn",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="40",id=670},src={"Sunken Treasure (5)"}}
E["quest:673"] = {t="quest",n="Foul Magics",z="arathi",s="Tor'gan in Hammerfall is sure that a powerful warlock lives within the walls of Stromgarde and uses an arcane relic to summon demons in large numbers. Following the first part of Foul Magics, he sends you to kill the warlock and bring back the relic.",h="Tor'gan in Hammerfall is sure that a powerful warlock lives within the walls of Stromgarde and uses an arcane...",sec={{t="A Warlock in Stromgarde",b="Tor'gan is certain that a warlock lives within Stromgarde's walls. Now and then the warlock uses an arcane relic to call up terrible demons in great numbers. The burning in Tor'gan's blood grows by the day. He wants the warlock found and killed, and whatever magical object is on the body brought to him, so that he can destroy it and keep its power from tainting the land. The warlock is Marez Cowl, and the object is a Befouled Bloodstone Orb.",sp=0},{t="What the Orb Recalls",b="With the orb destroyed, Tor'gan expects his restless nights to turn to peaceful sleep. To him it recalls the dreadful hold demons once had over the orcs, back before Hellscream freed them from their curse.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to hunt the warlock?",a="Tor'gan in Hammerfall sends you into Stromgarde to find the warlock and take the magical object they carry.",al={"who gives foul magics","foul magics quest giver","torgan quest"}},{q="Where is the warlock located?",a="Marez Cowl is within the walls of Stromgarde, outside the Keep itself and to the west, hiding behind a building. You can hear her channeling a spell.",al={"where is marez cowl","stromgarde warlock location","where to find marez cowl"}},{q="What relic are you sent to retrieve?",a="Marez Cowl's Befouled Bloodstone Orb, the magical object Tor'gan wants brought to him so he can destroy it.",al={"what item does torgan want","befouled bloodstone orb","foul magics item"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan want the warlock stopped?",a="The warlock has summoned terrible demons in large numbers. Tor'gan wants the source of that power removed and the orb destroyed so it cannot taint the land any longer.",al={"why destroy the orb","torgan motivation","why stop the warlock"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","hammerfall","marez cowl","stromgarde","torgan","warlock"},rel={"quest:671","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:stromgarde-keep","topic:warlock","zone:arathi"},m={start="Tor'gan",["end"]="Tor'gan",level="40",faction="Horde",id=673},src={"Foul Magics (2)"}}
E["quest:679"] = {t="quest",n="Call to Arms",z="arathi",s="Following the previous Call to Arms, Drum Fel at Hammerfall declares that it is time to strike the head from the beast. He sends you after the Boulderfist lords and shaman who lair in the ruins of Stromgarde.",h="Following the previous Call to Arms, Drum Fel at Hammerfall declares that it is time to strike the head from...",sec={{t="The Head of the Beast",b="Drum Fel says you have proven able enough to help deliver one last great blow. Those leading the attacks have made their lair in the ruins of Stromgarde, which he calls a symbol of human frailty. Hunt down the Boulderfist lords and the shaman who serve them, for they would try to drive the Horde out of these lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to fight the Boulderfist leaders?",a="Drum Fel, at the Horde outpost of Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who gives call to arms","drum fel quest","who starts call to arms 3"}},{q="Where are the Boulderfist lords and shaman located?",a="Drum Fel says those leading the attacks are holed up in the ruins of Stromgarde.",al={"where are boulderfist lords","boulderfist shaman location","where to find ogre leaders"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the chain?",a="It follows the previous Call to Arms and is the last step in the chain that begins with Tallow in Tarren Mill.",al={"what came before call to arms 3","call to arms chain","hammerfall ogre chain"}},{q="What does Drum Fel want done to the Boulderfist leaders?",a="He wants the lords and shaman leading the attacks killed as one last great blow, because they would drive the Horde from these lands.",al={"why kill boulderfist lords","why attack stromgarde ogres"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","boulderfist lords","boulderfist shaman","drum fel","hammerfall","stromgarde"},rel={"quest:677","subzone:hammerfall","npc:drum-fel","quest:680","quest:676","npc:tallow","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:arathi"},m={start="Drum Fel",["end"]="Drum Fel",level="40",faction="Horde",id=679},src={"Call to Arms (3)"}}
E["quest:680"] = {t="quest",n="The Real Threat",z="arathi",s="Following Call to Arms, Korin Fel tells you that her husband is unaware of why Hammerfall is under attack, and asks you to slay the ogre Or'Kalar and bring her his head.",h="Following Call to Arms, Korin Fel tells you that her husband is unaware of why Hammerfall is under attack...",sec={{t="A Grudge Against Her Husband",b="Korin Fel says you serve her husband well, yet he has no idea why Hammerfall is being attacked. The cause is Or'Kalar, Mug'thol's pawn in Stromgarde, who hates her husband for defeating him years ago and wants him dead. Her auguries tell her the ogre has set a trap for him.",sp=0},{t="What Korin Hides",b="Korin has hidden the signs of the ogre's presence from her husband, who she believes would rush off foolishly if he knew where Or'Kalar is. She asks for your help instead. You will find Or'Kalar near the Tower of Arathor, and she expects his death to end the attacks on Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Korin Fel trying to protect?",a="Her husband. Her auguries tell her Or'Kalar has set a trap for him, and the ogre wants him dead for defeating him years ago.",al={"korin husband","why does korin need help"}},{q="Why is Or'Kalar attacking Hammerfall?",a="Korin Fel calls Or'Kalar Mug'thol's pawn in Stromgarde, filled with hatred for her husband, who defeated him years ago. She says his death would stop the attacks.",al={"why does or'kalar hate korin's husband","who is or'kalar","or'kalar motive"}},{q="Where is Or'Kalar located?",a="Korin Fel says he is near the Tower of Arathor.",al={"or'kalar location","where to find or'kalar","find or'kalar"}},{q="Why does Korin keep the threat a secret from her husband?",a="She fears he would rush off foolishly if he learned where the ogre is, so she has kept him from seeing any trace of Or'Kalar.",al={"why keep it secret","why hide or'kalar","korin secret"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","korin fel","mug'thol","or'kalar","stromgarde","tower of arathor"},rel={"quest:677","quest:676","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:tower-of-arathor","zone:arathi"},m={start="Korin Fel",["end"]="Korin Fel",level="40",faction="Horde",id=680},src={"The Real Threat (Classic)"}}
E["quest:681"] = {t="quest",n="Northfold Manor",z="arathi",s="Captain Nials, at Refuge Pointe, asks for help against the Syndicate holding Northfold Manor. Their hold on the land between the defenders of Stromgarde and Southshore makes it hard for supplies to arrive.",h="Captain Nials, at Refuge Pointe, asks for help against the Syndicate holding Northfold Manor.",sec={{t="A Struggling Defense",b="Stromgarde has been carved up between the ogres, the Syndicate and the Alliance, and every faction fights the others to a bloody stalemate. The Alliance's forces dwindle while their enemies grow. The defenders need help from Southshore, but supplies are slow to arrive.",sp=0},{t="The Syndicate at the Manor",b="The Syndicate holds the ground between the defenders and Southshore. Captain Nials wants you to go to their base at Northfold Manor and cut down their highwaymen and mercenaries, in the hope that the pressure on the supply trains eases and more get through.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Captain Nials want the Syndicate attacked at Northfold Manor?",a="Southshore is where help must come from, but the Syndicate sits on the land between there and the defenders. Nials hopes that slaying them at their base will ease the pressure on the supply trains.",al={"why attack northfold manor","nials objective","purpose of northfold manor quest"}},{q="What is the current situation in Stromgarde?",a="The ogres, the Syndicate and the Alliance have divided the once great city between them, and each faction battles the others to a bloody stalemate. The Alliance's forces dwindle while its enemies grow.",al={"stromgarde war status","who controls stromgarde","state of stromgarde"}},{q="Where are the Alliance supplies coming from?",a="The defenders look to the town of Southshore for help, but the Syndicate's hold on the land between makes the supplies difficult to receive.",al={"who supplies refuge pointe","southshore supplies","where do shipments originate"}},{q="Which enemies need to be eliminated at the manor?",a="Ten Syndicate Highwaymen and six Syndicate Mercenaries, found at Northfold Manor.",al={"who to kill at northfold","northfold targets","syndicate enemies list"}}},kw={"captain nials","highwayman","mercenary","northfold manor","refuge pointe","southshore","stromgarde","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:northfold-manor","topic:syndicate","subzone:southshore","zone:arathi"},m={start="Captain Nials",["end"]="Captain Nials",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=681},src={"Northfold Manor (Classic)"}}
E["quest:682"] = {t="quest",n="Stromgarde Badges",z="arathi",s="In Stromgarde, the Syndicate is fighting a contingent of militia, and its leaders pay gold for every badge taken from a fallen militiaman. At Refuge Pointe, Captain Nials wants those badges recovered.",h="In Stromgarde, the Syndicate is fighting a contingent of militia, and its leaders pay gold for every badge...",sec={{t="A Bounty on Soldiers",b="In Stromgarde the Syndicate is at war with a contingent of militia. To push their followers into fighting the better-trained soldiers, Syndicate leaders pay gold for each badge taken from a slain militiaman. Captain Nials calls them cutthroats and will not let them keep trophies of the brave fallen, so you are sent into the Syndicate-held part of Stromgarde to hunt for the badges and bring them back to Refuge Pointe. Nials wants the Syndicate to learn it cannot profit from the dead.",sp=0},{t="After the Hunt",b="Nials promises that the relatives of the fallen will be told they died in battle. The news is grim to deliver, but Nials judges it better than leaving a family to wonder what became of a missing relative.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the Syndicate want Stromgarde badges?",a="Their leaders have put a bounty on the militia: gold for every badge taken from a militiaman who has fallen, meant to push the Syndicate's followers into fighting the better-trained troops.",al={"why syndicate badges","syndicate bounty stromgarde","why collect badges"}},{q="Where are the badges found?",a="Captain Nials sends you into the part of Stromgarde the Syndicate controls to hunt them for the badges.",al={"where to find badges","stromgarde badge location","badge drop location"}},{q="Who orders the retrieval of the badges?",a="Captain Nials, at Refuge Pointe, who does not want the Syndicate keeping trophies from the fallen militia.",al={"who gives stromgarde badges","captain nials badge quest","questgiver stromgarde badges"}}},kw={"arathi","badges","captain nials","militia","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","topic:syndicate","zone:arathi"},m={start="Captain Nials",["end"]="Captain Nials",level="37",id=682},src={"Classic quest text: Stromgarde Badges"}}
E["quest:687"] = {t="quest",n="Theldurin the Lost",z="arathi",s="A member of the Twilight's Hammer asks you to find Theldurin the Lost, who was once of their order, lost his mind, and fled with the scroll of Myzrael. Rumor places him in the Badlands.",h="A member of the Twilight's Hammer asks you to find Theldurin the Lost, who was once of their order, lost his...",sec={{t="The Man Who Stole the Scroll",b="Theldurin once belonged to the Twilight's Hammer, until his mind slipped and he turned his back on the order's teachings. As he fled, he took the scroll of Myzrael with him. Those he left behind could not catch him.",sp=0},{t="Rumors of the Badlands",b="The order has heard that Theldurin hides in the Badlands, raving and mad. The scroll is needed for the Lady's return, and to get it you must first find the man who took it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Theldurin the Lost?",a="A former member of the Twilight's Hammer who lost his mind, rejected the order's teachings, and fled with the scroll of Myzrael.",al={"theldurin backstory","who is theldurin","theldurin lore"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer looking for him?",a="He ran off with the scroll of Myzrael, which the order says must be found to bring the Lady back.",al={"why find theldurin","why do cultists want theldurin"}},{q="Where did Theldurin flee after leaving the order?",a="The order has only rumors, which place him in the Badlands.",al={"where is theldurin","theldurin location lore"}},{q="What comes directly before this search?",a="It follows Myzrael's Allies.",al={"previous quest theldurin","prereq for theldurin the lost"}}},kw={"badlands","gerrig bonegrip","myzrael","scroll of myzrael","theldurin","theldurin the lost","twilight's hammer","zaruk"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:badlands","zone:arathi"},m={start="Gerrig Bonegrip, Zaruk",["end"]="Theldurin the Lost",level="40",faction="Both",id=687},src={"Theldurin the Lost (quest)"}}
E["quest:688"] = {t="quest",n="Myzrael's Allies",z="arathi",s="Myzrael speaks through the keystone, declaring herself free but in hiding from her captors, and tells you to speak with Zaruk in Hammerfall, who knows how she can be summoned.",h="Myzrael speaks through the keystone, declaring herself free but in hiding from her captors, and tells you to...",sec={{t="Free but Hidden",b="Myzrael cries out that she is free. For now she must gather her strength out of sight of her captors, because if they faced her today they would overpower and imprison her again. In time, she vows, she will confront the giants who held her, and they will regret keeping her.",sp=0},{t="Zaruk of Hammerfall",b="Myzrael calls you a noble ally and says she will want your aid again in time. When she is ready, she will have you summon her to the surface. For now she sends you to Zaruk in Hammerfall, who knows how it can be done.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Zaruk?",a="Myzrael herself, speaking through the keystone, tells you to see Zaruk in Hammerfall.",al={"who gives myzraels allies","quest giver myzraels allies","who speaks through the keystone"}},{q="Why is Myzrael hiding?",a="She says her captors would overpower and imprison her again if they faced her now, so she hides while she gathers strength.",al={"why doesnt myzrael fight","why is myzrael weak","why does myzrael hide"}},{q="Where can Zaruk be found?",a="In Hammerfall.",al={"zaruk location","where is zaruk","find zaruk"}},{q="What role does Zaruk play for Myzrael?",a="Myzrael says he knows how she can be summoned.",al={"why talk to zaruk","what does zaruk know","zaruk purpose"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","giants","hammerfall","keystone","myzrael","zaruk"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi"},m={start="Keystone",["end"]="Zaruk",level="40",faction="Horde",id=688},src={"Myzrael's Allies (Horde)"}}
E["quest:691"] = {t="quest",n="Worth Its Weight in Gold",z="arathi",s="At Refuge Pointe, Apprentice Kryten is after Witherbark tusks, medicine pouches and a shadow hunter's knife, all reagents for Archmage Malin, who sent him and Skuerto to gather them. He asks you to seek them among the Witherbark trolls in the southeast of Arathi.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Apprentice Kryten is after Witherbark tusks, medicine pouches and a shadow hunter's knife...",sec={{t="Malin's Reagents",b="Archmage Malin sent Kryten and Skuerto to Arathi to collect reagents, and Kryten had no idea how to gather them until you arrived. He needs ten Witherbark tusks, four medicine pouches and one shadow hunter knife. The Witherbark trolls make their home in the southeast of Arathi.",sp=0},{t="What the Witherbark Carry",b="By Kryten's research, any Witherbark troll should have tusks, and the witch doctors carry the medicine pouches. The knife belongs to the mightiest shadow hunters, handed to them after they finish their rites of passage. Only battle will show which of them has one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apprentice Kryten working for?",a="Archmage Malin sent Kryten and Skuerto to Arathi to collect reagents for him.",al={"who sent kryten","kryten master","why is kryten in arathi"}},{q="Where are the Witherbark trolls located?",a="In the southeast of Arathi, where the Witherbark trolls make their home.",al={"witherbark location","where to find witherbark","witherbark village location"}},{q="Which trolls carry the medicine pouches?",a="Kryten's research says it is the Witherbark witch doctors who carry medicine pouches, while any Witherbark troll should have tusks.",al={"medicine pouch source","who has medicine pouches","witherbark medicine pouch"}},{q="How do you find the shadow hunter knife?",a="The mightiest Witherbark shadow hunters should have it, a blade handed to them after their rites of passage. Which of them carries one only battle will reveal.",al={"shadow hunter knife location","who drops shadow hunter knife","rite of passage knife"}}},kw={"apprentice kryten","arathi highlands","archmage malin","medicine pouch","refuge pointe","shadow hunter knife","skuerto","witherbark","witherbark tusk"},rel={"npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:witherbark-village","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},m={start="Apprentice Kryten",["end"]="Apprentice Kryten",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=691},src={"Worth Its Weight in Gold (Classic)"}}
E["quest:693"] = {t="quest",n="Wand over Fist",z="arathi",s="Skuerto at Refuge Pointe has worked out where the first of Trelane's items ended up. Kor'gresh has Trelane's Wand of Invocation in Boulderfist Hall, and Skuerto wants it brought back.",h="Skuerto at Refuge Pointe has worked out where the first of Trelane's items ended up.",sec={{t="The Ogre and the Wand",b="After your work for Apprentice Kryten, Skuerto has found where Trelane's first item went. Kor'gresh holds it in Boulderfist Hall, and has been throwing blasts of ice at his own kin to keep them in line. Skuerto reckons the ogre must be close to figuring out all of the wand's powers. Boulderfist Hall lies south of Refuge Pointe and then east of Thandol Span.",sp=0},{t="Skuerto's List",b="On your return, Skuerto counts the wand as one item down and three more to go, according to his list. The other three are all in Stromgarde.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Wand over Fist?",a="Skuerto, at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"wand over fist questgiver","who starts wand over fist","where to get wand over fist"}},{q="Where is Kor'gresh located?",a="Kor'gresh is in Boulderfist Hall, which lies south of Refuge Pointe and then east of Thandol Span.",al={"where is korgresh","korgresh location","find korgresh"}},{q="What item needs to be recovered?",a="Trelane's Wand of Invocation, the first of Trelane's items. Kor'gresh has been throwing blasts of ice at his kin with it.",al={"what item is kor'gresh holding","what wand","trelane wand"}},{q="What prerequisites are needed for this quest?",a="It follows Worth Its Weight in Gold, the work you did for Apprentice Kryten.",al={"wand over fist pre reqs","prerequisites for wand over fist","previous quest to wand over fist"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist hall","korgresh","refuge pointe","skuerto","stromgarde","thandol span","trelane","wand of invocation","wand over fist"},rel={"npc:skuerto","subzone:boulderfist-hall","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:thandol-span","zone:arathi"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Skuerto",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=693},src={"Wand over Fist (Classic)"}}
E["quest:694"] = {t="quest",n="Trelane's Defenses",z="arathi",s="With the wand in hand, Skuerto turns to the ogres that surround the Tower of Arathor. To bring the tower's defenses to life, he needs an azure agate from the Boulderfist shaman, to be taken to Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe.",h="With the wand in hand, Skuerto turns to the ogres that surround the Tower of Arathor.",sec={{t="The Tower's Defenses",b="Ogres surround the Tower of Arathor in Stromgarde. Skuerto says the tower's defenses must be activated if you are to stand a chance against them and still reach the items alive.",sp=0},{t="A Gem for a Key",b="Certain gems from the tower have caught the fancy of the Boulderfist shaman, who carried them off, though Skuerto says they will not keep them for long. Bring one azure agate to Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe, who knows the spell to enchant it so that it works as a key.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is an azure agate needed?",a="Skuerto wants the tower's defenses activated so you can face the ogres around the Tower of Arathor and still reach the items alive. Enchanted, the gem will work as a key.",al={"why azure agate","trelane defenses purpose","why get the gem"}},{q="Where did the azure agates come from?",a="The Boulderfist shaman carried them off from the Tower of Arathor and have grown fond of them.",al={"who took the agates","where are the gems from","agate origin"}},{q="Who can enchant the gem?",a="Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe knows the spell to enchant the gem so that it works as a key.",al={"who enchants the agate","kryten role","who turns it into a key"}}},kw={"apprentice kryten","azure agate","boulderfist shaman","refuge pointe","skuerto","stromgarde","tower of arathor","trelane's defenses"},rel={"npc:skuerto","quest:695","subzone:tower-of-arathor","subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","topic:shaman"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Apprentice Kryten",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=694},src={"Trelane's Defenses (Classic)"}}
E["quest:695"] = {t="quest",n="An Apprentice's Enchantment",z="arathi",s="Apprentice Kryten has enchanted the agate you brought him from the Boulderfist shaman. Touched to a pedestal at the foot of the tower, it will wake the tower's defenses. Before you leave, he sends you to Skuerto for the rest.",h="Apprentice Kryten has enchanted the agate you brought him from the Boulderfist shaman.",sec={{t="A Key for the Tower",b="Kryten hands you the enchanted gem. He explains that touching it to a pedestal at the foot of the tower will wake the tower's defenses, and that you should use it when you are ready to go in after the rest of Trelane's items. He will await your return at the camp. First, speak to Skuerto, who will fill in whatever else you need to know.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the enchanted agate?",a="Touched to a pedestal at the foot of the tower, it wakes the tower's defenses. You use it when you are ready to go in after the rest of Trelane's items.",al={"why do i need the agate","enchanted agate use","what does the gem do"}},{q="Who do you need to talk to before leaving camp?",a="Skuerto. Kryten tells you to speak to him before you leave, as he will fill in whatever else you need to know.",al={"who do i talk to","where to go next","who is skuerto"}},{q="Where will Kryten be?",a="He will be awaiting your return at the camp.",al={"where is kryten","kryten waiting"}}},kw={"apprentice kryten","arathi highlands","enchanted agate","skuerto","tower","trelane"},rel={"npc:skuerto","zone:arathi"},m={start="Apprentice Kryten",["end"]="Skuerto",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=695},src={"An Apprentice's Enchantment"}}
E["quest:696"] = {t="quest",n="Attack on the Tower",z="arathi",s="With the tower's defenses awake, Skuerto at Refuge Pointe sends you into the ogre-held tower for Trelane's phylactery, orb and ember agate. They should lie in chests inside, and Skuerto says Malin will be more than pleased if you bring them back.",h="With the tower's defenses awake, Skuerto at Refuge Pointe sends you into the ogre-held tower for Trelane's...",sec={{t="Into the Tower",b="After Kryten's enchantment, Skuerto tells you what to look for: Trelane's phylactery, orb and ember agate. The three should be sitting in chests inside the tower, and you should have no trouble opening them yourself, though the ogres call for care. The tower's defenses will not deal with them on their own, and if the ogres find you stealing from them, they will put the hurt on you.",sp=0},{t="Skuerto's Verdict",b="When you return the three items, Skuerto says Malin could not have asked for a worthier person to aid them here. Malin will be delighted to learn how completely their venture has succeeded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who assigns this task?",a="Skuerto, at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, once Kryten has enchanted the gem.",al={"who gives attack on the tower","quest giver attack on the tower","where to get attack on the tower"}},{q="What items are you sent to retrieve?",a="Trelane's phylactery, orb and ember agate. Each should be in a chest inside the tower.",al={"attack on the tower items","what relics to get","trelanes items"}},{q="What will the ogres do?",a="The tower's defenses will not take care of them for you. If the ogres find out you are stealing from them, they will put the hurt on you.",al={"are the ogres dangerous","tower ogres"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows An Apprentice's Enchantment, in which Kryten enchants the gem and sends you to Skuerto.",al={"attack on the tower prerequisite","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","attack on the tower","malin","ogres","refuge pointe","skuerto","trelane","trelane's ember agate","trelane's orb","trelane's phylactery"},rel={"npc:skuerto","subzone:refuge-pointe","quest:695","zone:arathi"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Skuerto",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=696},src={"Attack on the Tower (Classic)"}}
E["quest:697"] = {t="quest",n="Malin's Request",z="arathi",s="Skuerto gives you a sealed letter for Archmage Malin, who is found in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. It tells Malin that Kryten and Skuerto will be home soon, and Skuerto is certain Malin will repay you well for helping them in Arathi.",h="Skuerto gives you a sealed letter for Archmage Malin, who is found in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",sec={{t="A Letter for the Archmage",b="After the work in Arathi, Skuerto hands you a letter to take back to Stormwind. Its message for Archmage Malin in the Mage Quarter is that Kryten and Skuerto will be home soon. Skuerto has no doubt that Malin will repay you well for helping them, and sends you off with a wish for a safe journey.",sp=0},{t="Malin Reads the Letter",b="When Malin opens the letter, his eyes grow wide. He is delighted, and says Trelane will be so pleased. He supposes Kryten and Skuerto share his excitement now that they are heading home to Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you with the letter?",a="Skuerto does. The letter tells Malin that he and Kryten will be home soon.",al={"who gives the letter","who starts malins request","malins request starter"}},{q="Where is Archmage Malin located?",a="Archmage Malin is in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",al={"where is archmage malin","archmage malin location","where do i turn this in"}},{q="Who is Kryten?",a="Kryten is Skuerto's companion in the Arathi Highlands. Skuerto says the two of them will be home soon.",al={"who is kryten","kryten arathi"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="It follows Attack on the Tower, the work Skuerto asked of you at the tower in Arathi.",al={"previous quest","prereq","what leads to this"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","archmage malin","kryten","mage quarter","malin's request","sealed letter","skuerto","stormwind"},rel={"npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:arathi","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:mage"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Archmage Malin",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=697},src={"Malin's Request (2)"}}
E["quest:702"] = {t="quest",n="Guile of the Raptor",z="arathi",s="After the earlier Guile of the Raptor, Tor'gan hands you an orb and sends you to Gor'mul at Hammerfall. Its energy carries the essence of the raptor, meant to stir Gor'mul's spirit and give him new purpose.",h="After the earlier Guile of the Raptor, Tor'gan hands you an orb and sends you to Gor'mul at Hammerfall.",sec={{t="Tor'gan's Orb",b="Tor'gan gives you an orb whose energy is meant to fill Gor'mul with the raptor's essence. He hopes it will rouse the warrior's spirit and set him on a fresh course in life. Once Gor'mul is himself again, Tor'gan means to explain the current state of the Horde to him and gain a great warrior's help in the unceasing battles.",sp=0},{t="Gor'mul's Bitterness",b="Gor'mul greets your return with sourness, saying he wants nothing more than more of Tor'gan's pity and mocking you with talk of brightly colored string.",sp=0},{t="A Strange Power",b="Still, the orb is something more interesting than what Gor'mul expected, and he remarks on the strange power it gives off.",sp=1},{t="The Raptor Within",b="As Gor'mul takes the orb, his blood stirs and the raptor's guile slips through him. He wonders aloud whether this is the shamanism Tor'gan spoke of, and then declares himself renewed, his strength returning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gor'mul?",a="Gor'mul is a despondent warrior at Hammerfall. Tor'gan wants to lift his spirits and set him on a new course, so that the Horde can have a great warrior's help.",al={"who is gormul","gormul lore","what is wrong with gormul"}},{q="What is the purpose of Tor'gan's Orb?",a="Its energy is meant to fill Gor'mul with the raptor's essence, rousing his spirit and giving him fresh purpose.",al={"what does the orb do","torgan orb purpose","guile orb"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="An earlier Guile of the Raptor comes first, and this step builds on it.",al={"previous quest","prereq"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","gor'mul","hammerfall","raptor essence","tor'gan","torgan's orb"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","quest:701","zone:arathi","topic:horde","topic:warrior"},m={start="Tor'gan",["end"]="Gor'mul",level="37",faction="Horde",id=702},src={"Guile of the Raptor (2)"}}
E["quest:847"] = {t="quest",n="Guile of the Raptor",z="arathi",s="After Tor'gan's orb gave Gor'mul the raptor's essence, the power he felt has him wondering about the shamans' magic. He sends you to tell Tor'gan he has been convinced, for the time being, and will listen.",h="After Tor'gan's orb gave Gor'mul the raptor's essence, the power he felt has him wondering about the shamans'...",sec={{t="A Warrior Convinced",b="Gor'mul wonders aloud whether the power coursing through him is the shamans' power that Tor'gan tried to show him. He finds it interesting. He asks you to tell Tor'gan that he has been convinced, for the time being, and will hear what Tor'gan has to say.",sp=0},{t="Tor'gan's Reply",b="Tor'gan says he will speak with Gor'mul once the enchantment wears off. He thanks you for helping bring Gor'mul back among the living, and expects that Gor'mul is grateful as well.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Tor'gan?",a="Gor'mul does. After feeling the power of the orb, he asks you to tell Tor'gan that he has been convinced, for the time being.",al={"who starts guile of the raptor 3","who gives this quest","where does this start"}},{q="Why does Gor'mul change his mind about Tor'gan?",a="He wonders whether the power he felt is the shamans' power that Tor'gan tried to show him, and he finds it interesting. He is convinced for the time being and will listen to Tor'gan.",al={"why did gormul change his mind","gormul shaman magic","is gormul convinced"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="It follows the earlier step in which you brought Tor'gan's orb to Gor'mul.",al={"previous quest","prereq guile of the raptor"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","gor'mul","guile of the raptor","hammerfall","shaman","tor'gan"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","topic:shaman","zone:arathi"},m={start="Gor'mul",["end"]="Tor'gan",level="37",faction="Horde",id=847},src={"Guile of the Raptor (3)"}}
E["subzone:boulder-gor"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulder'gor",z="arathi",s="Boulder'gor is a rugged hill in the western Arathi Highlands, situated directly north of the ruined human kingdom of Stromgarde. It serves as an active encampment for the Boulderfist ogres and their unusual allies among the Witherbark forest trolls.",h="Boulder'gor is a rugged hill in the western Arathi Highlands, situated directly north of the ruined human...",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres and Trolls",b="Rising just north of the crumbling ramparts of Stromgarde Keep, Boulder'gor is a steep bluff claimed by the Boulderfist clan. Within its shadows sits the Boulderfist Outpost mound, making it a central bastion of ogre power across the highlands. Uniquely, the ogres here share their fires and fortifications with forest trolls of the Witherbark tribe, including shadowy spellcasters who lend their dark magic to the clan's brute force. This mutual cooperation poses an ongoing danger to any travelers passing along the central roads of Arathi.",sp=0},{t="Surrounding Territory",b="The slopes around Boulder'gor look down over the open highlands of western Arathi. Hemmed between the Syndicate-infiltrated ruins of Stromgarde and the wild elemental sites of the plains, Boulder'gor remains a heavily guarded and hostile stronghold of tribal solidarity against both Alliance and Horde wanderers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Boulder'gor?",a="Boulder'gor is an elevated hill and encampment north of Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands. It is heavily inhabited by Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark forest trolls.",al={"where is bouldergor","bouldergor info","what is this place"}},{q="Why are forest trolls living alongside ogres here?",a="The Witherbark trolls and Boulderfist ogres maintain a pragmatic alliance in Arathi. Both seek to maintain dominance over the highlands and fend off rival factions, pooling troll shadowcraft with brute ogre strength.",al={"why are trolls here","witherbark ogre alliance","trolls and ogres"}},{q="What major landmarks are near Boulder'gor?",a="Boulder'gor sits directly north of Stromgarde Keep, and the ogre mound of Boulderfist Outpost lies within the hill itself.",al={"nearby places","what is next to bouldergor","landmarks"}},{q="Is Boulder'gor friendly to the Horde or Alliance?",a="Neither. The Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark trolls of Boulder'gor are entirely hostile to both the Alliance and the Horde, aggressively defending their hill from outsiders.",al={"can i go there safely","is bouldergor hostile"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls visiting the highlands will find no kinship here: the Witherbark forest trolls of Boulder'gor harbor deep ancient grudges against all outsiders, including other troll tribes.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces seeking to reclaim Stromgarde, Boulder'gor represents a serious threat lurking right on the fallen kingdom's northern doorstep."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulder'gor","boulderfist","bouldergor","ogres","stromgarde","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:boulderfist-outpost","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Boulder'gor"}}
E["subzone:boulderfist-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderfist Hall",z="arathi",s="Boulderfist Hall is a heavily fortified ogre mound nestled in the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands, just north of Thandol Span. It serves as the local stronghold for the Boulderfist ogres, who exert their brute influence across the neighboring trade routes and valleys under the command of Kor'gresh Coldrage.",h="Boulderfist Hall is a heavily fortified ogre mound nestled in the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Brute Strength",b="Carved into the rugged southern bluffs of the Arathi Highlands, Boulderfist Hall is the principal redoubt of the Boulderfist clan in the region. Sheltered within its earthen ramparts and deep caverns, ogre brutes and magi maintain a fortified settlement mere steps from Witherbark Village and the strategic bridge at Thandol Span. Deep within the mound lurks their regional chieftain, Kor'gresh Coldrage, alongside enforcers like Phalanax. From this stronghold, the ogres project violent control over the surrounding roads, making any peaceful transit between Arathi and the Wetlands perilous for travelers and supply caravans alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Boulderfist Hall?",a="It is a fortified ogre mound and cave complex in the southern Arathi Highlands, serving as the base of operations for the Boulderfist clan in this territory.",al={"what is this place","boulderfist mound","ogre cave arathi"}},{q="Who rules Boulderfist Hall?",a="The stronghold is led by the ogre chief Kor'gresh Coldrage, who directs his clan from the deep cavern inside the mound alongside champions like Phalanax.",al={"who leads boulderfist hall","ogre boss arathi","kor'gresh"}},{q="Why is this location strategically important?",a="Its proximity to Thandol Span allows the Boulderfist ogres to threaten the vital overland route connecting the Arathi Highlands to Khaz Modan, choking off traffic and preying on travelers.",al={"why ogres here","thandol span danger"}},{q="Are the Boulderfist allied with the nearby Witherbark trolls?",a="No formal alliance is recorded. The Boulderfist ogres and the forest trolls of Witherbark Village dwell in close proximity, and elsewhere in the highlands, at Boulder'gor, Witherbark trolls even share ground with the ogres. Both remain hostile to outsiders of every faction.",al={"ogres and trolls friends","witherbark alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Positioned just above Thandol Span, the Boulderfist ogres pose a constant ambush hazard for Alliance couriers and reinforcements moving north from Ironforge into Arathi.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Arathi Highlands requires breaking the independent power of the ogres, clearing the southern ridge to safeguard Horde movement from Hammerfall."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","boulderfist hall","kor'gresh coldrage","ogre mound","phalanax","thandol span"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:witherbark-village"},src={"Boulderfist Hall"}}
E["subzone:boulderfist-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderfist Outpost",z="arathi",s="Boulderfist Outpost is a fortified mound nestled deep within the ogre settlement of Boulder'gor in the Arathi Highlands. Serving as an interior den and holding area, it houses aggressive Boulderfist ogres alongside a few Witherbark trolls.",h="Boulderfist Outpost is a fortified mound nestled deep within the ogre settlement of Boulder'gor in the Arathi...",sec={{t="A Stronghold within the Mound",b="Carved into the earth and stone of western Arathi, Boulderfist Outpost functions as the heart of Boulder'gor. While brute enforcers dominate the settlement above, the outpost's interior concentrates the clan's core strength and provides a dark subterranean shelter. A handful of Witherbark troll witch doctors occasionally mingle among the ogres here, hinting at tenuous tribal cooperation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderfist Outpost located?",a="Boulderfist Outpost is an interior mound found within the larger ogre settlement of Boulder'gor, situated in the western expanses of the Arathi Highlands.",al={"boulderfist outpost location","where is boulderfist outpost","boulderfist mound entrance"}},{q="Why are there trolls inside an ogre outpost?",a="Witherbark forest trolls dwell nearby in the Arathi Highlands and occasionally share ground with the Boulderfist ogres. A few Witherbark witch doctors can be found practicing their craft within the depths of the outpost alongside the ogres.",al={"why are witherbark here","trolls in boulderfist","witherbark trolls arathi"}},{q="Who is imprisoned in the outpost?",a="No named captives are known to be held in the outpost today. Its damp corridors belong to Boulderfist enforcers and a few Witherbark witch doctors, and anyone wandering inside should expect a fight rather than a rescue.",al={"boulderfist prisoners","who is trapped in boulderfist","captives in arathi ogres"}},{q="Who leads the ogres inside the outpost?",a="While the clan's brute enforcers patrol the interior, an exceptionally fierce ogre named Kovork is known to lurk within the mound as a notable threat.",al={"kovork","boulderfist boss arathi","boulderfist rare"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts traveling Arathi should give the mound a wide berth, as the Boulderfist enforcers inside attack any intruder on sight.",["faction:Horde"]="The Boulderfist ogres make no distinction between factions, attacking Horde wanderers just as readily as their Alliance rivals."},kw={"arathi","boulder'gor","boulderfist","captives","kovork","ogre mound","prisoners","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:boulder-gor","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Boulderfist Outpost"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-east-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of East Binding",z="arathi",s="The Circle of East Binding is a mysterious ancient ritual site situated in the eastern reaches of the Arathi Highlands, just southwest of Hammerfall. Anchored by the Stone of East Binding, the site is violently contested and guarded by roaming water elementals known as cresting exiles.",h="The Circle of East Binding is a mysterious ancient ritual site situated in the eastern reaches of the Arathi...",sec={{t="The Eastern Ward",b="Positioned amidst the rugged highlands east of Stromgarde, the Circle of East Binding is one of several ancient sites of power scattered across the Arathi basin. At its focal point stands the Stone of East Binding, an enigmatic monument radiating potent elemental magic. Swirling water elementals known as cresting exiles roam the surrounding earth and fiercely defend the stone against any mortals who dare approach.",sp=0},{t="Elemental Imprisonment",b="The stones throughout Arathi are not mere natural anomalies; they function as ancient binding wards intended to suppress and imprison volatile elemental forces. The restless water spirits surrounding the eastern circle betray the strain on these wards, as the entities drawn to or trapped by the stone's magic lash out at travelers and adventurers navigating the nearby road to Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Circle of East Binding located?",a="The Circle of East Binding is located in the eastern region of the Arathi Highlands, south of the main road and slightly southwest of the Horde encampment of Hammerfall.",al={"east binding location","where is circle of east binding","circle of east binding map"}},{q="What creatures are found here?",a="The circle is overrun by aggressive water elementals, the cresting exiles that relentlessly guard the Stone of East Binding.",al={"east binding mobs","what monsters are at east binding","cresting exiles"}},{q="Why are there water elementals in the highlands?",a="The stones scattered across Arathi serve as ancient elemental bindings. The presence of water elementals here points to the containment or attraction of aqueous elemental energy channeled through the eastern ward stone.",al={"why water elementals arathi","east binding elemental lore"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Stone of East Binding?",a="The Stone of East Binding is part of a coordinated network of binding stones throughout the Arathi Highlands designed to anchor, channel, and lock away volatile elemental entities.",al={"stone of east binding purpose","what does east binding stone do"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The binding stones in Arathi represent crude or ancient methods of elemental suppression, contrasting sharply with a shaman's pursuit of elemental balance and communion.",["faction:Horde"]="Lying just down the road from Hammerfall, the volatile water spirits around the circle pose an ongoing territorial nuisance for Horde patrols and supply lines."},kw={"arathi highlands","circle of east binding","cresting exile","elementals","hammerfall","stone of east binding"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall"},src={"Circle of East Binding"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-inner-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of Inner Binding",z="arathi",s="The Circle of Inner Binding is an ancient ring of ritual stones situated in the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands, just east of Stromgarde Keep. Guarded by hostile earth elementals, it holds the Stone of Inner Binding, the most potent seal used to restrain the imprisoned elemental princess Myzrael deep beneath the earth.",h="The Circle of Inner Binding is an ancient ring of ritual stones situated in the southern hills of the Arathi...",sec={{t="The Core Seal",b="Perched upon a plateau south of the main road, the Circle of Inner Binding anchors the strongest of the ancient wards sealing Myzrael beneath Arathi. Towering slabs surround the central Stone of Inner Binding, which thrums with dense geo-magical power. Enormous rumbling earth elementals patrol the stones relentlessly, drawn to the site's resonance or bound as guardians. Despite these potent wards, cracks in this inner seal permit the trapped entity beneath the Highlands to reach out telepathically, whispering pleas for freedom to unsuspecting wanderers who handle shards of its stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Circle of Inner Binding?",a="The Circle houses the Stone of Inner Binding, which acts as the primary and strongest ward anchoring the subterranean prison of Myzrael. It works alongside other elemental circles scattered throughout the Arathi Highlands to keep the creature restrained beneath the surface.",al={"why is this circle here","what does the inner binding do","circle of inner binding lore"}},{q="What creatures guard this circle?",a="The circle is heavily guarded by powerful earth elementals, primarily Rumbling Exiles. These rocky behemoths aggressively attack anyone who approaches the ritual stones.",al={"what enemies are here","inner binding mobs","rumbling exile"}},{q="Who is whispering through the stone?",a="The voice reaching out through the binding shard belongs to Myzrael, an ancient and powerful elemental princess imprisoned deep beneath the earth. Her psychic reach has managed to pierce through this fractured seal to contact mortal minds.",al={"who talks to you here","myzrael voice","whispering stone"}},{q="Where is the Circle of Inner Binding located?",a="It is located in the southern portion of the Arathi Highlands, situated on the elevated ridgeline just east of the ruined stronghold of Stromgarde Keep.",al={"inner binding location","where is circle of inner binding","how to find inner binding"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The raw earthen energy surging through the Circle of Inner Binding indicates ancient, heavy elemental bonds, though the unnatural agitation of the local earth spirits warns of corruption beneath the soil.",["class:Mage"]="The geometric arrangement of the stones forms an intricate, long-lasting containment field capable of channeling and anchoring immense subterranean magical pressures."},kw={"arathi highlands","circle of inner binding","earth elementals","myzrael","rumbling exile","stone of inner binding","stromgarde keep"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep"},src={"Circle of Inner Binding"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-west-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of West Binding",z="arathi",s="The Circle of West Binding is one of several ancient ritual sites scattered across the Arathi Highlands, situated near Thoradin's Wall. Centered around the Stone of West Binding, this arcane ring is overrun by fiery elemental entities bound to the site.",h="The Circle of West Binding is one of several ancient ritual sites scattered across the Arathi Highlands...",sec={{t="The Western Keystone",b="Tucked against the rugged slopes near Thoradin's Wall, the Circle of West Binding forms part of a wider network of ritual sites dispersed throughout the Arathi Highlands. At its heart sits the Stone of West Binding, an ancient relic tied to elemental containment. The grounds are swarming with Burning Exiles—volatile fire elementals that relentlessly guard the perimeter, making any approach to the stone a perilous endeavor for travelers traversing the western plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Circle of West Binding?",a="It is an ancient ritual site in western Arathi Highlands, located near Thoradin's Wall. It holds the Stone of West Binding and is fiercely guarded by hostile fire elementals.",al={"circle of west binding","stone of west binding","west binding circle"}},{q="Why are there fire elementals here?",a="The Burning Exiles inhabit and guard the Stone of West Binding. They are elemental forces drawn or bound to the ancient magical foci constructed across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"burning exiles arathi","why fire elementals west binding","elementals circle of west binding"}},{q="Who is Ruul Onestone?",a="Ruul Onestone is a Boulderfist ogre mage who prowls the site, a rare and dangerous brute rather than a scholar of the binding stone.",al={"ruul onestone","ruul","dwarf at west binding"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The binding stones of Arathi offer arcane practitioners insight into how ancient mages and shamans anchored and subdued planar elemental entities.",["class:Shaman"]="The volatile presence of the Burning Exiles reveals the lingering elemental unrest tethered to these ancient Arathi keystones."},kw={"arathi highlands","burning exile","circle of west binding","elemental","ruul onestone","stone of west binding","thoradin's wall"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:thoradin-s-wall"},src={"Circle of West Binding"}}
E["subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Crypt (Stromgarde Keep)",z="arathi",s="Deep within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep lies the royal crypt, situated past the sanctum chapel in the heart of the district held by the surviving Stromgarde defenders. It holds the tomb of the fallen King Thoras Trollbane and the ancestral treasures of his dynasty. Guarded closely by Prince Galen and faithful caretakers, the vault remains a sanctuary of royal honor amid a shattered kingdom.",h="Deep within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep lies the royal crypt, situated past the sanctum chapel in the heart...",sec={{t="The Tomb of Thoras Trollbane",b="Hidden beneath the Sanctum of Stromgarde Keep, this subterranean burial vault serves as the final resting place of King Thoras Trollbane, the warrior monarch who led Stromgarde through the Second War. Despite the devastation engulfing the city—split among Syndicate rogues and Boulderfist ogres—the remaining Stromgarde militia fiercely maintains their grip on this quarter. Prince Galen Trollbane personally watches over the crypts alongside dedicated royal caretakers, ensuring his father's body and legacy remain undisturbed by the scavengers and enemies outside.",sp=0},{t="The Vault of Trol'kalar",b="Beyond housing the royal dead, the crypt safeguards prized artifacts belonging to the Trollbane lineage. Chief among these relics is Trol'kalar, the ancient runed greatsword forged centuries ago to slay trolls. Entrusted to the sworn protection of caretakers such as Alaric, Nevlin, and Weston, the chamber and its treasures are secured with powerful safeguards. Galen and his loyalists guard the tomb relentlessly, well aware that rival factions and hostile trolls across Arathi would covet the blade's ancient power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is buried in the crypt?",a="King Thoras Trollbane, the late ruler of Stromgarde, is interred here. His son, Prince Galen Trollbane, keeps watch over the tomb amidst the ruined city.",al={"who is buried here","whose tomb is this","crypt tomb"}},{q="What is Trol'kalar?",a="Trol'kalar is an ancient heirloom blade belonging to the Trollbane family. Its name translates from the ancient tongue to mean 'troll slayer,' and it was originally forged to fight the forest trolls of the Arathi basin.",al={"trolkalar sword","trollbane sword","what is trolkalar"}},{q="Who guards the crypt?",a="The crypt is defended by Prince Galen Trollbane and the Stromgarde royal caretakers, including Alaric, Nevlin, and Weston. They protect the burial chamber from encroaching Syndicate thieves and Boulderfist ogres.",al={"crypt guards","who defends the crypt","caretakers"}},{q="Where is the crypt located?",a="It is located within Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands, found deep inside the Sanctum district behind the keep's chapel, in the sector still held by Stromgarde loyalists.",al={"crypt location","how to find the crypt","where is stromgarde crypt"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, the tomb represents the tragic decline of Stromgarde, one of the seven great kingdoms, and the hallowed grave of one of the Alliance's fiercest wartime leaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stromgarde's royal crypt stands as one of the last bastions of Alliance heritage in Arathi, guarded tenaciously against bandits, ogres, and the Horde."},kw={"arathi","crypt","galen","sanctum","stromgarde","thoras","trol'kalar","trollbane"},rel={"subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi"},src={"Crypt (Stromgarde Keep)"}}
E["subzone:dabyrie-s-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Dabyrie's Farmstead",z="arathi",s="Dabyrie's Farmstead is an Alliance-aligned rural settlement situated in northern Arathi Highlands. In a realm shattered by the Third War and overrun by Syndicate outlaws and Witherbark trolls, this estate remains a stubborn bastion of Stromgarde citizens led by Kenata Dabyrie.",h="Dabyrie's Farmstead is an Alliance-aligned rural settlement situated in northern Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Highlands",b="Perched in the northern fields of the Arathi Highlands, Dabyrie's Farmstead is one of the very few functioning human homesteads remaining in the fractured kingdom of Stromgarde. Owned by Kenata Dabyrie and worked alongside her sons, Fardel and Marcel, the grounds are fiercely defended by a local family militia. Surrounded by aggressive wildlife, opportunistic bandits, and the nearby Forsaken presence in the north, the farm stands as a symbol of human endurance in a ruined land.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Feuds",b="Survival in Arathi rarely comes without bitter enmity. The estate has drawn the intense ire of the Forsaken, particularly Genavie Callow, a former noblewoman who lost her lands and kin during the Third War. Callow accuses the surviving Dabyrie clan of looting her family's precious heirlooms in the chaos of the plague, transforming the modest farmstead into a target of vengeful Horde mercenaries seeking to settle old northern grudges.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dabyrie's Farmstead?",a="The farm is the home of Kenata Dabyrie and her sons, Fardel and Marcel. They are human citizens of Stromgarde loyal to the Alliance, protected by a sworn local militia.",al={"who owns dabyrie farm","dabyrie family","kenata dabyrie"}},{q="Why is the Horde targeting this farm?",a="A Forsaken woman named Genavie Callow harbors a grudge against the Dabyries. She claims they plundered her family's estate and made off with her surviving heirlooms while her own relatives perished in the Third War.",al={"why kill dabyrie","genavie callow quest","horde dabyrie quest"}},{q="Is Dabyrie's Farmstead part of Stromgarde?",a="Yes. The Dabyries consider themselves subjects of the kingdom of Stromgarde and allies of the broader Alliance, holding fast despite the collapse of their central capital to the south.",al={"is dabyrie alliance","stromgarde farm"}},{q="What threats surround the farmstead?",a="The farm sits dangerously close to hostile highlands predators, roaming Syndicate cutthroats, and Forsaken forces pressing down across the borders from the north.",al={"threats to dabyrie","danger near dabyrie farm"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the farmstead is a rare and comforting reminder that Stromgarde's people still survive and fight for their land amidst encroaching enemies.",["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, the prosperous homestead is an irritating spectacle of living humans hoarding goods looted from families who perished during the Third War."},kw={"arathi","callow","dabyrie","fardel","farmstead","kenata","marcel","stromgarde"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance","topic:third-war","topic:syndicate"},src={"Dabyrie's Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:drowned-reef"] = {t="subzone",n="Drowned Reef",z="arathi",s="The Drowned Reef is a treacherous stretch of coastal waters off the southern cliffs of the Arathi Highlands. Beneath the waves lie ancient sunken ruins, claimed by hostile Daggerspine naga who appear able to control the bay's tides, endangering passing vessels.",h="The Drowned Reef is a treacherous stretch of coastal waters off the southern cliffs of the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships",b="Just outside the hidden entrance to Faldir's Cove, the Drowned Reef forms a watery graveyard for navigators. Shattered ships, including the Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine, lie submerged beneath the waves. Daggerspine naga led by Prince Nazjak inhabit the reef and appear able to control the bay's tides, dooming crews seeking refuge in the cove.",sp=0},{t="The Sunken City",b="Those brave or foolish enough to dive into the deep water will discover the submerged architecture of an ancient elven city. Calcified elven gems remain among its drowned ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Drowned Reef?",a="The Drowned Reef is a hazardous marine zone along the southern coast of the Arathi Highlands, situated just offshore from Faldir's Cove. It is known for its shallow, ship-breaking shoals and ancient ruins lurking beneath the sea.",al={"drowned reef","where is drowned reef","arathi reef"}},{q="Why are there so many sunken ships here?",a="The reef is dangerous to ships navigating the southern Arathi coast. Its Daggerspine naga appear able to control the bay's tides, endangering crews trying to find refuge in Faldir's Cove.",al={"why are ships sinking","sunken ships arathi","maidens folly"}},{q="Who controls the Drowned Reef?",a="The reef is inhabited by the Daggerspine tribe of naga, who dwell within the flooded ruins. Their local forces are directed by Prince Nazjak, who commands them to prey upon stranded sailors and protect their submerged territory.",al={"who leads the naga here","prince nazjak","daggerspine naga arathi"}},{q="What are the ruins submerged beneath the reef?",a="The reef contains the ruins of an ancient elven city, with calcified elven gems among its submerged remains.",al={"underwater ruins arathi","elven ruins drowned reef"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The flooded halls beneath the reef and the calcified gems resting in the seabed are somber reminders of the Kaldorei empire that shattered into the sea ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering."},kw={"arathi highlands","daggerspine","drowned reef","faldir's cove","maiden's folly","naga","prince nazjak","spirit of silverpine","sunken ruins"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:faldir-s-cove","topic:naga"},src={"Drowned Reef"}}
E["subzone:drywhisker-gorge"] = {t="subzone",n="Drywhisker Gorge",z="arathi",s="Drywhisker Gorge is a rugged cleft in the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, situated northeast of the Horde outpost of Hammerfall. The gorge and its inner cavern are held by a hostile clan of kobolds, who fiercely guard rich mineral deposits and ancient elemental relics buried deep underground.",h="Drywhisker Gorge is a rugged cleft in the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, situated northeast of...",sec={{t="A Warren in the Eastern Crags",b="Tucked away in the mountainous folds east of Hammerfall, Drywhisker Gorge serves as the primary redoubt of the Drywhisker clan of kobolds. While kobolds are often dismissed as simple mine pests, the Drywhiskers in Arathi are heavily entrenched. They guard their subterranean passages with fierce territorial tenacity, working veins of rare Lesser Bloodstone Ore and defending the deep recesses of the earth. Their proximity makes them a persistent nuisance to the nearby orcs of Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Deep Cavern",b="Venture far enough past the torchlit barricades and winding tunnels, and the cavern reveals a darker secret than ordinary pickaxes and candles. Allied with the towering stone giants of the highlands, the Drywhisker kobolds attend to motes of ancient earth magic. Deep in the heart of the cave lies a mysterious stone shard that houses a trapped fragment of the essence of Princess Myzrael, an ancient earth entity bound below the surface.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives in Drywhisker Gorge?",a="The gorge and its cavern network are inhabited by the Drywhisker clan of kobolds. They aggressively defend their territory from outsiders, guarding both their mining operations and ancient relics hidden within.",al={"drywhisker gorge inhabitants","what is in drywhisker gorge","who controls drywhisker gorge"}},{q="Where is Drywhisker Gorge located?",a="The gorge cuts through the craggy eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, directly northeast of the Horde settlement of Hammerfall. A rugged path leads up through the hills east of the outpost to reach the cavern entrance.",al={"how to get to drywhisker gorge","drywhisker gorge location","where is the cave in arathi"}},{q="What makes the cave inside significant?",a="Beyond containing rare deposits of Lesser Bloodstone Ore, the cave shelters an ancient stone shard. This relic contains a fragment of the imprisoned essence of Princess Myzrael, a powerful subterranean entity.",al={"what is in the cave","drywhisker cave secrets","myzrael shard"}},{q="Why are the kobolds allied with mountain giants?",a="The Drywhisker clan shares a connection with the local stone giants, serving and guarding the earth relics and elemental motes tied to the bindings of Princess Myzrael deep beneath Arathi.",al={"kobolds and giants","why are drywhiskers with giants"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners prize the Drywhisker cavern as the only known source of Lesser Bloodstone Ore, a dense, crimson-veined mineral embedded deep within the kobold-infested rock.",["faction:Horde"]="Resting right over the mountain ridge from Hammerfall, the hostile Drywhisker kobolds represent an unpredictable threat lingering on the outpost's eastern flank."},kw={"arathi highlands","drywhisker","drywhisker gorge","hammerfall","kobold","lesser bloodstone ore","princess myzrael","stone shard"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall","topic:kobold"},src={"Drywhisker Gorge"}}
E["subzone:faldir-s-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Faldir's Cove",z="arathi",s="Faldir's Cove is a secluded natural harbor nestled along the southern coastline of the Arathi Highlands. Steeped in human history, it is traditionally remembered as the departure point from which early settlers sailed south to found Stormwind. Today, it serves as an emergency shelter for stranded Blackwater Raiders whose fleet ran afoul of local hazards.",h="Faldir's Cove is a secluded natural harbor nestled along the southern coastline of the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Gateway South and a Pirate Haven",b="Tucked away behind the rugged bluffs south of Stromgarde Keep, Faldir's Cove is linked to the mainland by a concealed cave tunnel. The cove honors the memory of Faldir, the ancient Arathor explorer whose expedition set sail from these very shores to cross the Great Sea and establish the southern kingdom of Stormwind. In the present day, however, its quiet waters house a very different crowd: an expedition of Blackwater Raiders from Booty Bay, led by Captains Steelgut and O'Breen, who sailed north pursuing ancient elven treasures only to end up trapped in the bay.",sp=0},{t="The Wreck of the Blackwater Fleet",b="The Blackwater venture turned catastrophic upon reaching the Arathi coast. Strange and unnatural tides conjured by the territorial naga dwelling on the offshore Drowned Reef shattered two of their three vessels. Only the Harbinger survived intact, limping into Faldir's Cove. With the naga prowling the waters and their navigation charts resting beneath the waves, the surviving pirates and their gnomish researchers find themselves marooned, reliant on neutral travelers to battle the aquatic horrors and recover sunken salvage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Faldir?",a="Faldir was an ancient pioneer from the early human empire of Arathor. He and his followers embarked from this coastal haven to sail across the seas, journeying south to establish the settlements that eventually became the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"faldir lore","who is faldir","faldir founder"}},{q="How do you reach Faldir's Cove?",a="The cove is reached by finding a hidden tunnel passage located just southeast of the outer southern walls of Stromgarde Keep. Walking through this subterranean tunnel brings travelers directly out onto the secluded shore.",al={"how to get to faldir's cove","faldir cove entrance","cave to faldirs cove"}},{q="Why are the Blackwater Raiders here?",a="Captain Steelgut and Captain O'Breen led an expedition north from Booty Bay in search of sunken elven treasures. Along with gnomish inventors who designed gem-detecting apparatuses, they aimed to salvage precious relics calcified within the offshore reefs.",al={"why are pirates here","blackwater raiders arathi","what are the pirates doing"}},{q="What happened to their ships?",a="Two of the expedition's three vessels were destroyed by unnatural tides stirred up by hostile naga inhabiting the Drowned Reef. Only the flagship Harbinger safely made port in the cove, leaving the crew stranded without their sunken charts.",al={"why are ships wrecked","sunken ships arathi","who sank the ships"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Standing upon these shores connects humans to their early heritage, marking the historic launching point where the ancestors of Stormwind parted from the ancient empire of Arathor.",["race:Gnome"]="The camp features Doctor Draxlegauge and Professor Phizzlethorpe, who have deployed ingenious engineering contraptions to analyze and extract elven gems from calcified coastal reefs."},kw={"blackwater raiders","captain o'breen","captain steelgut","draxlegauge","drowned reef","faldir","faldir's cove","harbinger","phizzlethorpe"},rel={"subzone:drowned-reef","zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:booty-bay","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:naga"},src={"Faldir's Cove"}}
E["subzone:go-shek-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Go'Shek Farm",z="arathi",s="Go'Shek Farm is an agricultural outpost in the eastern Arathi Highlands, occupied by the Horde and guarded by orcs from Hammerfall. Behind its mundane rural facade, Forsaken apothecaries conduct secretive alchemical experiments far from prying eyes.",h="Go'Shek Farm is an agricultural outpost in the eastern Arathi Highlands, occupied by the Horde and guarded by...",sec={{t="A Horde Outpost in the East",b="Go'Shek Farm is held by the Horde. Positioned south of Hammerfall and just north of the hostile Witherbark troll territory, the farmstead nominally serves as a vital supply and staging hub for the orcish settlement. Hammerfall Grunts patrol the fields and stables, securing food and livestock to sustain the Horde's embattled foothold in the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="The Apothecary's Workshop",b="Beneath the routine work of tilling soil and tending beasts lies a darker purpose. The Royal Apothecary Society has established a quiet presence at the farmstead, led by figures such as Apothecary Jorell. Couriers slip between Go'Shek Farm and Tarren Mill, ferrying notes, reagents, and research into early variants of the Forsaken's new plague. The Alliance has taken notice, dispatching scouts to intercept these messengers and uncover the nature of the poison brewing in the Arathi soil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde occupying Go'Shek Farm?",a="The farmstead provides essential agricultural supplies and livestock for the nearby orc stronghold of Hammerfall. Additionally, it gives the Forsaken a discreet, guarded staging ground to conduct sensitive chemical and alchemical research.",al={"who owns goshek farm","why are orcs at goshek farm","goshek farm horde"}},{q="Who used to own this farm?",a="The farm's earlier owners are not recorded. Today it belongs to the Horde, worked and guarded by orcs from nearby Hammerfall.",al={"goshek farm history","human farm arathi","primwell skye"}},{q="What kind of experiments are happening here?",a="Forsaken apothecaries conduct secretive alchemical work at the farm. Alliance agents are trying to uncover its nature by investigating courier traffic and records kept there.",al={"apothecary jorell","plague experiments arathi","forsaken research goshek"}},{q="Why are there Alliance agents watching the farm?",a="Quae and Kinelory are investigating suspicious traffic between the farmstead and Tarren Mill. They seek evidence of the Forsaken's activities and need help reaching it.",al={"quae kinelory","alliance scouting goshek","hints of a new plague"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The farm supports Hammerfall and houses Forsaken apothecaries whose secretive work has attracted Alliance scrutiny.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the farm is critical to keeping Hammerfall provisioned, while also maintaining a heavily fortified perimeter against the encroaching Witherbark trolls."},kw={"apothecary jorell","arathi","go'shek farm","goshek","hammerfall","kinelory","quae","swee","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","subzone:tarren-mill","quest:367","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:witherbark-village","topic:alliance"},src={"Go'Shek Farm"}}
E["subzone:hammerfall"] = {t="subzone",n="Hammerfall",z="arathi",s="Hammerfall is the Horde's primary fortified outpost in the Arathi Highlands, built upon the ruins of a notorious Alliance internment camp. It honors the legendary former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell nearby while fighting to liberate his captive people. Today, orcs and Forsaken garrison the settlement against hostile Boulderfist ogres, Witherbark trolls, and the League of Arathor.",h="Hammerfall is the Horde's primary fortified outpost in the Arathi Highlands, built upon the ruins of a...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Liberation",b="Following the Second War, the human Alliance built vast internment camps across Lordaeron to contain the defeated orcs. The compound that once stood here was among the largest. Years later, Thrall and Orgrim Doomhammer assaulted the camp to liberate the lethargic captives. During the chaos of their retreat, a charging Alliance knight drove a lance through Doomhammer's backplate, mortally wounding the legendary Warchief. Following the Third War, the new Horde reclaimed the ruined ground and established an outpost here, naming it Hammerfall in memory of their fallen leader.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold in the Highlands",b="Today, Hammerfall serves as the Horde's lifeline in Arathi. Positioned against hostile surroundings, the garrison contends with aggressive Boulderfist ogres from Boulder'gor and Boulderfist Hall, as well as the native Witherbark trolls. Furthermore, Forsaken Defilers have made the outpost their staging ground to claim the contested resources of the Arathi Basin against the Alliance's League of Arathor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this base called Hammerfall?",a="It is named in honor of former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who was mortally wounded on this ground by an Alliance knight's lance during the liberation of the orc internment camp.",al={"why hammerfall","hammerfall name origin","who died at hammerfall"}},{q="What was Hammerfall before the Horde rebuilt it?",a="It was one of the largest Alliance of Lordaeron internment camps, constructed after the Second War to imprison captive orcs.",al={"hammerfall history","what was hammerfall before","internment camp arathi"}},{q="Who leads the defense of Hammerfall right now?",a="The orc Drum Fel rules Hammerfall and coordinates the outpost's defense, directing Horde champions against the encroaching Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark forest trolls. Tallow, a Forsaken warrior at Tarren Mill, first sends recruits to strike at the Boulderfist ogres of Boulder'gor.",al={"hammerfall leaders","who is in charge of hammerfall","tallow drum fel"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken stationed here?",a="The Forsaken Defilers operate out of Hammerfall to secure vital supplies from the Arathi Basin and counter the Alliance's League of Arathor.",al={"forsaken hammerfall","why are undead in hammerfall","defilers arathi"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Hammerfall is hallowed ground for orcs, marking the place where Orgrim Doomhammer gave his life to free captive clanmates and pass the mantle of Warchief to Thrall.",["faction:Horde"]="Surrounded by hostile ogres, forest trolls, and remnants of the Alliance, Hammerfall is the Horde's sole fortress ensuring control over the central Arathi Highlands."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","defilers","hammerfall","internment camp","orgrim doomhammer","thrall","witherbark"},rel={"npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:arathi","npc:thrall","npc:drum-fel","npc:tallow","subzone:boulder-gor","subzone:boulderfist-hall","topic:second-war"},src={"Hammerfall"}}
E["subzone:northfold-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Northfold Manor",z="arathi",s="Northfold Manor is a dilapidated agricultural estate situated on the northwestern fringes of the Arathi Highlands. Once a prosperous human homestead before the collapse of Stromgarde, the grounds are now occupied by criminal operatives of the Syndicate engaging in unsettling, dark practices.",h="Northfold Manor is a dilapidated agricultural estate situated on the northwestern fringes of the Arathi...",sec={{t="A Den of Brigands",b="Perched on the rolling highlands near the Thoradin's Wall passage, Northfold Manor once supported the kingdom of Stromgarde. In the chaos following the realm's fracturing, displaced Alteraci nobility and outlaws of the Syndicate claimed the manor house, barn, and fields as an operational base. Instead of tending crops, Syndicate mercenaries, highwaymen, and pathstalkers use the farmstead to stage ambushes along the roads and coordinate their presence across Arathi.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Undertones",b="Behind the everyday thievery and armed posturing, Northfold Manor harbors more sinister pursuits. Lingering traces of demonic summoning cling to the farmstead, felt keenly by sensitive spellcasters and shamans in the region. Discarded bloodstone amulets—potent talismans used to fuel dark invocations—litter the grounds, indicating that the Syndicate rogues here are entangling themselves with demonic magic far beyond simple banditry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Northfold Manor?",a="The estate has fallen into the hands of the Syndicate, an organization of dispossessed Alteraci nobles, bandits, and rogue mercenaries who now use the property as an armed encampment.",al={"who lives here","who owns northfold","syndicate farm"}},{q="What dark magic is being practiced here?",a="Visitors sensitive to magical energies detect residual traces of demonic summoning. The Syndicate forces stationed at the manor possess bloodstone amulets, used to channel and assist in dangerous demonic rituals.",al={"demons at northfold","bloodstone","what are they summoning"}},{q="Why does the Horde care about this farm?",a="The troll shaman Tor'gan at Hammerfall sensed an unnatural disturbance brewing across the highlands. Investigating the source led him directly to Northfold Manor, prompting the Horde to investigate the Syndicate's occult activities.",al={"horde interest northfold","why tor'gan cares"}},{q="Who is Singer?",a="Singer is an elusive Syndicate figure occasionally spotted lurking inside the main house of Northfold Manor among the other brigands.",al={"singer","singer rare","who is singer"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The shamans of Hammerfall closely watch Northfold Manor, dispatching warriors to seize the bloodstone talismans the Syndicate uses to dabble in demonic summoning.",["class:Shaman"]="The demonic residue lingering over Northfold Manor disrupts the natural elements, causing spiritual unease and fiery rage in attuned shamans who draw near."},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","northfold manor","singer","stromgarde","syndicate","tor'gan"},rel={"topic:syndicate","zone:arathi","topic:horde","quest:255","topic:troll"},src={"Northfold Manor"}}
E["subzone:refuge-pointe"] = {t="subzone",n="Refuge Pointe",z="arathi",s="Refuge Pointe is the primary redoubt for the Alliance and the surviving remnants of Stromgarde within the Arathi Highlands. Perched centrally along the highlands' trade road, it serves as a staging ground to reclaim the shattered capital of Stromgarde Keep and hold back rival forces across the region.",h="Refuge Pointe is the primary redoubt for the Alliance and the surviving remnants of Stromgarde within the...",sec={{t="A Bastion for Stromgarde's Remnants",b="Following the devastation of the Third War and the catastrophic fall of Stromgarde Keep, the bulk of Stromgarde's surviving populace fled south toward friendlier lands. Those who remained formed a resolute vanguard, digging in at Refuge Pointe under Captain Nials. Composed of battle-hardened Stromgarde soldiers, League of Arathor forces, and supporting Alliance specialists, the encampment represents the kingdom's last organized stand in its ancestral homeland.",sp=0},{t="Stretched to the Limit",b="Refuge Pointe is constantly on the brink of being overwhelmed. Hemmed in by the Forsaken and the Horde based out of Hammerfall, Witherbark trolls, Syndicate rogues, and Boulderfist ogres, the garrison has zero reserves to spare. When dwarven commanders at the battered Thandol Span desperately requested reinforcements to fight off the Dark Iron clan, Captain Nials had to refuse. Every sword, shield, and scrap of supply stationed at Refuge Pointe must remain dedicated to defending the highlands and preparing a counteroffensive to retake Stromgarde Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Alliance presence here so small?",a="The kingdom of Stromgarde fell into ruin following the Third War, forcing most surviving civilians to evacuate south. The troops at Refuge Pointe are an embattled remnant of the Stromic army, bolstered by an expeditionary Alliance force. With supplies stretched thin and enemies on every front, they can barely hold their fortified camp.",al={"why is refuge pointe small","why so few soldiers","alliance numbers arathi"}},{q="Why won't Refuge Pointe send soldiers to help at the Thandol Span?",a="When dwarven messengers arrived asking for troops to defend Dun Modr and the Thandol Span from Dark Iron assaults, Captain Nials had to decline. With Stromgarde Keep overrun and hostile forces surrounding them, duty and survival demand that every soldier stay committed to holding the highlands and retaking their fallen capital.",al={"why no help dun modr","captain nials thandol span","plea to the alliance quest"}},{q="Who commands the camp?",a="Captain Nials commands the garrison at Refuge Pointe. She directs Stromgarde's military operations across the highlands, coordinating scouting efforts, skirmishes against the Syndicate and ogres, and defensive patrols along the main road.",al={"refuge pointe leader","who is in charge here","captain nials"}},{q="What is the League of Arathor?",a="The League of Arathor is an Alliance coalition committed to reclaiming the Arathi Highlands and securing vital resources in the neighboring Arathi Basin. Operating alongside Stromgarde's remnant forces at Refuge Pointe, they fight to deny the Forsaken-led Defilers control of the fertile valley.",al={"league of arathor","who are league of arathor","arathi basin alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Refuge Pointe serves as your sole military sanctuary and flight hub in the Arathi Highlands, offering critical relief in a dangerous territory contested by ogres, the Syndicate, and the Horde.",["race:Human"]="For humans, Refuge Pointe is a poignant reminder of Stromgarde's former glory as humanity's martial heartland, where stalwart defenders refuse to abandon their homeland despite overwhelming odds."},kw={"arathi highlands","arathor","captain nials","league of arathor","refuge pointe","stromgarde","thandol span"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","topic:alliance","npc:longbraid-the-grim","npc:skuerto","topic:third-war"},src={"Refuge Pointe"}}
E["subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Sanctum (Stromgarde Keep)",z="arathi",s="The Sanctum is a sacred redoubt tucked behind the chapel within Stromgarde Keep. Sheltered within the crumbling fortress, it guards the entrance to the ancestral Trollbane family crypt and stands as one of the few remaining bastions of the Holy Light amidst Arathi's ruin.",h="The Sanctum is a sacred redoubt tucked behind the chapel within Stromgarde Keep.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Ruins",b="While much of Stromgarde Keep has fallen to Syndicate infiltrators and the Boulderfist ogres, the Sanctum and its adjacent chapel have remained under the fierce protection of the surviving Stromgarde defenders. Located behind the house of worship, the Sanctum borders the citadel's graveyard and marks the threshold to the royal crypt where the kings of Stromgarde rest. For the battered loyalists rallying around Prince Galen Trollbane, holding this hallowed ground represents more than a tactical foothold; it is a desperate fight to keep their kingdom's ancestral heritage and faith from being trampled by invaders.",sp=0},{t="Threshold of the Kings",b="Beneath the stone flags of the Sanctum lies the passage into the royal tomb. The ground here is consecrated, intended as a place of peaceful reflection and worship of the Holy Light. In the wake of King Thoras Trollbane's murder and the kingdom's subsequent collapse, the Sanctum has instead become a defensive retreat. Those seeking to breach the inner sanctum must contend not only with the royal guards garrisoned throughout the halls, but with the haunting reality of an ancient human lineage clinging to survival on its sacred threshold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sanctum?",a="The Sanctum is the inner area behind the Church of Light's chapel within Stromgarde Keep. It adjoins the keep's graveyard and leads directly into the ancestral Trollbane family crypt.",al={"what is sanctum","stromgarde sanctum","sanctum stromgarde keep"}},{q="Who controls the Sanctum right now?",a="The Sanctum is held by surviving Stromgarde soldiers loyal to the Alliance and Prince Galen Trollbane. Unlike the rest of the ruined city overrun by Syndicate bandits and Boulderfist ogres, the chapel and Sanctum remain under human guard.",al={"who is in the sanctum","sanctum guards","who holds the sanctum"}},{q="What lies beyond the Sanctum?",a="Past the Sanctum lies the Trollbane family crypt, where the fallen rulers of Stromgarde, including the recently slain King Thoras Trollbane, are entombed.",al={"where does sanctum lead","sanctum crypt","what is behind the sanctum"}},{q="Why is this area important to Stromgarde?",a="Beyond serving as a consecrated center of worship for the Holy Light, the Sanctum protects the royal resting place of Stromgarde's kings. For the surviving defenders, surrendering it would mean allowing invaders to desecrate their ancestors' graves.",al={"why care about sanctum","sanctum significance","why is sanctum defended"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The chapel and Sanctum represent the last undefiled sanctuaries of the Holy Light within the fallen capital of Arathi, making its defense a matter of solemn duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="Holding the Sanctum ensures the royal line of Trollbane retains a grasp on their ancestral seat, keeping the Alliance presence alive in the contested ruins of Stromgarde."},kw={"arathi","chapel","church of light","crypt","galen","sanctum","stromgarde","trollbane"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:light","topic:alliance"},src={"Sanctum (Stromgarde Keep)"}}
E["subzone:stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Stromgarde Keep",z="arathi",s="Stromgarde Keep is the battered, divided capital of the fallen human kingdom of Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands. Once the proud cradle of human civilization known as Strom, the fortress is now partitioned between hostile Syndicate rogues, invading Boulderfist ogres, and a desperate remnant of royal defenders under Prince Galen Trollbane.",h="Stromgarde Keep is the battered, divided capital of the fallen human kingdom of Stromgarde in the Arathi...",sec={{t="Cradle of Humanity",b="Long before it bore its current name, this fortress was founded nearly three millennia ago as Strom, the first capital of the unified human empire of Arathor under King Thoradin. It served as the staging ground for humanity's victory against the forest trolls and was the birthplace of human wizardry, where high elven magi tutored the first hundred human spellcasters. Over centuries, as younger sister kingdoms like Dalaran, Lordaeron, and Stormwind rose and prospered, Strom's influence waned. Renamed Stromgarde by the stubborn Trollbane dynasty who stayed behind, it remained a proud warrior bastion throughout the Second War, anchoring the Alliance of Lordaeron against the Orcish Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Shattered Bastion",b="Following the devastation of the Third War, Stromgarde finally buckled under mounting catastrophes and treachery. Today, the majestic stone city sits fractured into three warring sectors. The aristocratic traitors of the Syndicate occupy the grand inner keep, while brutish Boulderfist ogres have overrun the former sanctum of the mage district. Pinned in the remaining quarter, Prince Galen Trollbane and the battered Stromgarde military wage a grueling, bloody war on multiple fronts just to keep their ancestral home from vanishing into memory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Stromgarde Keep right now?",a="The ruined city is carved into three fiercely contested zones. The treacherous Syndicate controls the central inner keep, invading Boulderfist clan ogres occupy the ruined mage district, and Prince Galen Trollbane leads the surviving remnants of the Stromgarde army from the remaining quarter.",al={"who lives in stromgarde","who owns stromgarde keep","who is in stromgarde"}},{q="What was the Empire of Arathor?",a="The Empire of Arathor was the very first unified human nation, founded nearly three thousand years ago by King Thoradin. Its capital was Strom, situated on the very grounds where Stromgarde Keep stands today.",al={"what is strom","first human kingdom","arathor empire"}},{q="Why is the city in ruins?",a="Stromgarde stood as a powerhouse through the Second War, but the kingdom was left vulnerable and isolated in the chaotic aftermath of the Third War. A combination of internal betrayal, opportunistic attacks by the criminal Syndicate, and assaults from Boulderfist ogres shattered the city's defenses.",al={"why is stromgarde destroyed","what happened to stromgarde"}},{q="Who is Galen Trollbane?",a="Prince Galen Trollbane is the royal scion and commander of Stromgarde's surviving forces. From his embattled redoubt inside the keep, he directs the desperate defense against both the Syndicate and the ogres.",al={"prince trollbane","who is prince galen"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Stromgarde was the ancient heart of your entire race, where the first human tribes banded together under Thoradin and learned the arcane arts from the high elves. Seeing it overrun by criminals and ogres is a bitter sight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stromgarde was a founding member of the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War. Its beleaguered defenders represent one of the last loyal strongholds left in the north, fighting desperately to avoid total annihilation."},kw={"arathi","arathor","boulderfist","galen","strom","stromgarde","stromgarde keep","syndicate","thoradin","trollbane"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:lordaeron","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Stromgarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:thandol-span"] = {t="subzone",n="Thandol Span",z="arathi",s="The Thandol Span is a pair of colossal dwarven stone bridges connecting the Wetlands of Khaz Modan with the Arathi Highlands of southern Lordaeron. Long celebrated as a marvel of engineering and the vital artery between the northern and southern kingdoms, it is currently in a state of disaster following a sabotage attack by Dark Iron infiltrators.",h="The Thandol Span is a pair of colossal dwarven stone bridges connecting the Wetlands of Khaz Modan with the...",sec={{t="The Fight for the Crossing",b="The surviving bridge remains contested and heavily guarded. Mountaineers from Ironforge fight desperately to preserve the remaining roadway and repel Dark Iron sappers, suffering painful losses in the process. The loss of the bridge would leave northern trade and military movements almost entirely reliant on maritime routes, cutting off Alliance forces stationed across the Arathi Highlands from immediate reinforcement.",sp=0},{t="A Lifeline Severed",b="Constructed following the War of the Three Hammers to bridge Ironforge with the Wildhammer clan of the Aerie Peak, the Thandol Span stands among the grandest stonecraft feats of dwarven history. Capable of supporting entire marching armies, it served as the critical land corridor between Lordaeron and Khaz Modan throughout the Second War, notably carrying Sir Anduin Lothar's counter-offensive southward. Today, the crossing is grievously wounded. Dark Iron saboteurs led by Balgaras the Foul and Kam Deepfury mounted a devastating assault from nearby Dun Modr, shattering one span entirely with explosives and threatening to sever overland travel between the allied realms completely.",sp=1,bt={"q303.3"}}},faq={{q="What is the Thandol Span?",a="It is a massive dwarven double-arched stone bridge spanning the deep canyon between the Wetlands in northern Khaz Modan and the Arathi Highlands in southern Lordaeron.",al={"thandol span overview","what is this bridge","thandol bridge"},it="place"},{q="Why is one of the bridges broken?",a="Dark Iron dwarves launched an assault from the captured outpost of Dun Modr, using high explosives to demolish one of the two spans in an attempt to cut Alliance supply lines.",al={"who blew up the bridge","thandol span destroyed","why is thandol span broken"},it="ruin"},{q="Why was the Thandol Span originally built?",a="Ironforge dwarves built the span after the War of the Three Hammers to foster trade, diplomacy, and enduring ties with their Wildhammer cousins living across the canyon in the north.",al={"who built thandol span","thandol history","why was it built"},it="origin"},{q="Did armies cross here during the Second War?",a="Yes. Although the Old Horde bypassed the bridges by crossing the sea to invade Lordaeron, Sir Anduin Lothar later led the Alliance counter-offensive across the Span to drive the orcs back into Khaz Modan.",al={"thandol span second war","orcs at thandol span","lothar thandol span"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Thandol Span?",a="The Thandol Span is held and guarded by the dwarves of Ironforge. Despite suffering brutal raids and sabotage from Dark Iron infiltrators operating out of nearby Dun Modr, Ironforge mountaineers continue to defend the surviving bridge, keeping open the vital link between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms.",al={"who controls thandol span","who runs thandol span","thandol span guards"},it="residents",add="6e9af8e2"},{q="Is the Thandol Span dangerous?",a="Yes, traveling across the Span is hazardous. Dark Iron saboteurs recently infiltrated the gorge and detonated explosives, completely severing one of the two twin arches and leaving the remaining span vulnerable. Hostile Dark Iron dwarves linger nearby in the northern Wetlands and around Dun Modr, actively plotting further strikes against travelers and Ironforge defenders holding the line.",al={"is thandol span safe","thandol span danger","threats at thandol span"},it="danger",add="a33b8b45"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the dwarves of Ironforge, the Span represents both a masterwork of their stonemasons and a painful battleground where Dark Iron kin have brought destruction to their front door.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Span is the sole direct overland link uniting Khaz Modan with the beleaguered northern outposts of Lordaeron, making its defense vital to the war effort."},kw={"arathi highlands","balgaras","dark iron","dun modr","ironforge","kam deepfury","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","zone:wetlands","zone:arathi","quest:631","quest:303","quest:378","npc:kam-deepfury","topic:second-war"},src={"Thandol Span"}}
E["subzone:thoradin-s-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Thoradin's Wall",z="arathi",s="Thoradin's Wall is a monumental, crumbling stone rampart dividing the Arathi Highlands from the Hillsbrad Foothills. Commissioned millennia ago by King Thoradin during the dawn of the Empire of Arathor, it was built to shield early humanity from the fierce incursions of the Amani trolls.",h="Thoradin's Wall is a monumental, crumbling stone rampart dividing the Arathi Highlands from the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Bulwark of Ancient Arathor",b="Erected nearly three thousand years ago, Thoradin's Wall marks the western frontier of ancient Strom, the heart of the first unified human empire. King Thoradin recognized that humanity's fledgeling settlements were acutely vulnerable to the predatory raids of the Amani forest trolls. By raising this vast stone barrier across the valley corridor, Arathor secured its heartland and forged a defensible bastion from which humanity could survive and eventually contest troll supremacy in the north.",sp=0},{t="Centuries of Decay",b="Today, the ancient barrier stands in severe disrepair. Vast breeches gash the stone ramparts, their battlements weathered down by thousands of years of exposure, warfare, and abandonment. Following the splintering of Arathor into rival kingdoms and the eventual fall of neighboring Lordaeron to the Scourge, no central realm maintains the masonry. Now, travelers and roaming bandits slip freely through its broken archways as they journey between Hillsbrad and the untamed Arathi Highlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built Thoradin's Wall?",a="It was commissioned by King Thoradin, the founder and warlord who unified humanity's tribes to establish the Empire of Arathor nearly three millennia ago.",al={"who made thoradins wall","creator of thoradins wall","thoradin wall origins"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the wall built in the first place?",a="King Thoradin ordered its construction to defend humanity's early capital, Strom, and its fledgling settlements from the fierce raids of the neighboring Amani troll empire.",al={"purpose of thoradins wall","why build the wall","what was thoradins wall for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the wall so broken down today?",a="The wall has suffered thousands of years of natural weathering, conflict, and neglect. After the Empire of Arathor splintered into independent human nations, the grand frontier fortification lost its strategic priority and was left to decay.",al={"why is thoradin wall broken","who destroyed thoradins wall","why ruined"},it="ruin"},{q="What regions does Thoradin's Wall separate?",a="The wall forms the natural overland border separating the lush Hillsbrad Foothills to the west from the rugged Arathi Highlands to the east.",al={"where is thoradins wall","what does the wall divide","border of thoradins wall"}},{q="What is Thoradin's Wall?",a="Thoradin's Wall is an ancient, colossal stone rampart that spans the border between the Arathi Highlands and Hillsbrad Foothills. Raised millennia ago during the height of the Empire of Arathor, it served as humanity's grand defensive bulwark to shield the heartlands around Strom from the fierce incursions of the Amani trolls. Today, though heavily weathered and broken, its towering arches and crumbling stones still loom over the trade road.",al={"what is thoradins wall","thoradin wall info","about thoradins wall"},it="place",add="b3263746"},{q="What happened at Thoradin's Wall?",a="For generations, the wall held firm against countless raids by the forest trolls of Zul'Aman, defending humanity's cradle. Over subsequent centuries, neglect, wars, and the sheer passage of time saw its defenses decay into the ruins standing today.",al={"history of thoradins wall","thoradins wall battles","what happened here"},it="history",add="a3fa6dab"},{q="Why is it called Thoradin's Wall?",a="The wall is named in honor of High King Thoradin, the legendary warlord who first unified the warring human tribes into the glorious Empire of Arathor. Shortly after establishing his empire and founding its great capital of Strom, Thoradin ordered the construction of this vast fortification to secure mankind's survival against hostile wilderness threats, ensuring his name remained etched in stone across the frontier.",al={"why is it called thoradins wall","who is thoradins wall named after","thoradin wall name"},it="name",add="bb7d6206"}},ang={["race:Human"]="Standing before the wall is a solemn brush with human antiquity, showcasing the enduring masonry of King Thoradin, who first unified the scattered human tribes.",["race:Troll"]="The ruined fortifications are a stark reminder of the ancient territorial wars where humanity successfully halted the domain of the forest trolls."},kw={"amani","arathi","arathor","hillsbrad","strom","thoradin","thoradin's wall","wall"},rel={"zone:arathi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:troll","topic:dwarf","topic:syndicate"},src={"Thoradin's Wall"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-arathor"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Arathor",z="arathi",s="The Tower of Arathor is a ruined wizard's tower situated in the former mage district in the southwestern reaches of Stromgarde Keep. Once the workshop of Archmage Trelane, it was overrun during the fall of the city and is currently occupied by Boulderfist ogres.",h="The Tower of Arathor is a ruined wizard's tower situated in the former mage district in the southwestern...",sec={{t="A Bastion Overrun",b="Erected in the heart of Stromgarde Keep's mage district and named after the ancient Empire of Arathor, this spire long served the realm's sorcerers. Its most notable resident, Archmage Trelane, devised a magical defensive grid keyed to enchanted gemstones to protect the sanctum. However, when the Syndicate and the Boulderfist ogre clan assaulted Stromgarde following the Third War, the kingdom fractured. Despite Trelane's desperate attempts to hold the tower using his arcane wards, the sheer brutish force of the ogres overwhelmed him. Forced to flee the city for his life, the archmage left behind his most prized arcane artifacts, leaving the spire in the hands of the Boulderfist brute Ruul Onestone and his followers.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Lost Relics",b="Even in exile, Trelane refused to abandon his life's work. Enlisting the aid of his former pupil, Archmage Malin of the Kirin Tor, an expedition was mounted to retrieve his phylactery, orb, and ember agate from the ruins. Operating out of Refuge Pointe, Malin's agents discovered that the ogres had pillaged the stones required to command the tower's automated defenses. By crafting a replacement enchanted agate and placing it upon the pedestals framing the tower's threshold, conjured water elementals could be awakened to purge the ogre occupiers and allow daring adventurers to recover the archmage's heirlooms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Arathor?",a="It is a mage tower located in the southwestern ruins of Stromgarde Keep. Named in honor of the ancient human empire of Arathor, it served as a center of study for the kingdom's mages until it fell to invading ogres.",al={"tower of arathor","stromgarde mage tower","arathi tower"}},{q="Who lives in the tower now?",a="The tower and the surrounding mage district are occupied by Boulderfist ogres. Inside the spire dwells the ogre mage Ruul Onestone along with his guards, who have rooted out and guarded the relics left behind by its former master.",al={"who is in the tower of arathor","tower of arathor mobs","tower of arathor boss"}},{q="Who was Archmage Trelane?",a="Archmage Trelane was a prominent wizard of Stromgarde who lived and studied in the tower. He created its gemstone-powered warding systems and fled into exile after failing to defend the sanctum against the Boulderfist assault.",al={"archmage trelane","who owned the tower","trelane"}},{q="How do the tower's defenses work?",a="Trelane keyed the tower to activate when an enchanted agate is placed against the pedestals flanking its entrance. When activated, the arcane matrix conjures hostile water elementals that battle any intruders occupying the entrance.",al={"how to activate tower defenses","trelane's defenses","tower pedestals"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The tower serves as a sobering reminder of what happened to Stromgarde's arcane enclave, while showcasing Archmage Trelane's clever mastery over defensive elemental constructs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stromgarde Keep is contested ground; helping Archmage Malin's agents recover Trelane's lost artifacts denies potent magical relics to the encroaching Boulderfist clan."},kw={"arathi","boulderfist","malin","ruul onestone","skuerto","stromgarde","tower of arathor","trelane"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","quest:690","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance","topic:third-war"},src={"Tower of Arathor"}}
E["subzone:witherbark-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Witherbark Village",z="arathi",s="Witherbark Village is a forest troll settlement nestled around a secluded lake in the southeastern hills of the Arathi Highlands. Inhabited by the hostile Witherbark tribe, it serves as a staging ground for troll raiders contesting both the Alliance remnants of Stromgarde and the Horde outpost at Hammerfall.",h="Witherbark Village is a forest troll settlement nestled around a secluded lake in the southeastern hills of...",sec={{t="Stronghold of the Forest Trolls",b="Built along the shores of a quiet mountain lake, Witherbark Village houses the fierce forest trolls of the Witherbark tribe. While fishers, axe throwers, and witch doctors occupy the hut-lined waterfront, tribal leaders such as Zalas Witherbark and deadly shadow hunters oversee operations from a massive cavern cavern tucked behind the settlement. The Witherbark maintain an opportunistic alliance with the Boulderfist ogres of Arathi, working together to carve out territory across the highlands—even establishing a firm foothold amidst the ruins of Stromgarde Keep. Fiercely territorial, they lash out at any outsider venturing into their corner of the basin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Witherbark Village?",a="The settlement is held by the Witherbark tribe, a faction of forest trolls indigenous to the region. They field headhunters, axe throwers, fishers, and witch doctors who defend the lake and surrounding paths.",al={"who are witherbark","witherbark trolls","who controls witherbark village"}},{q="What is inside the large cave behind the village?",a="The cavern serves as the seat of tribal leadership. Chieftain Zalas Witherbark and dangerous shadow hunters coordinate the tribe's raids and defenses from deep within its tunnels.",al={"witherbark cave","cave behind witherbark village","zalas witherbark location"}},{q="Why are the Witherbark trolls working with ogres?",a="The Witherbark have struck a loose alliance of convenience with the local Boulderfist ogres. Combining their strength allows them to press against the weakened human defenders of Stromgarde and threaten regional rivals like the Horde in Hammerfall.",al={"witherbark ogre alliance","trolls and boulderfist","why are trolls allied with ogres"}},{q="Are the Witherbark friendly to the Horde?",a="No. Like most Amani-descended forest trolls, the Witherbark harbor bitter resentment toward the modern Horde and its Darkspear trolls, and they fight the Horde at Hammerfall. They will attack Horde travelers on sight.",al={"are witherbark horde","can horde talk to witherbark","witherbark reputation"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Witherbark show no deference to the new Horde, frequently clashing with scouts from Hammerfall and threatening travel through the eastern passes.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls will find no kinship here; the forest trolls of the Witherbark view jungle trolls and the Horde with deep-seated hostility."},kw={"arathi highlands","forest trolls","nimar the slayer","witherbark","witherbark village","zalas witherbark"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall","topic:troll","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Witherbark Village"}}
E["zone:arathi"] = {t="zone",n="Arathi Highlands",z="arathi",s="The Arathi Highlands are a rugged plateau in southeastern Lordaeron, renowned as the ancient birthplace of the Empire of Arathor. Today, the kingdom of Stromgarde lies in ruins, leaving the craggy realm engulfed in multi-front warfare between the remnants of Stromgarde, the Horde, criminal Syndicate nobles, and invading ogres.",h="The Arathi Highlands are a rugged plateau in southeastern Lordaeron, renowned as the ancient birthplace of...",sec={{t="Cradle of Humanity",b="Millennia ago, King Thoradin united the fractured human tribes under the banner of the Arathi, constructing the majestic capital of Strom across these dry, defensible plains. It was here that humanity forged its legendary compact with the high elves during the Troll Wars, mastering the arcane arts to push back the Amani. Over time, noble bloodlines migrated north into Lordaeron and south toward Stormwind, but the imperial guard stayed behind to form the martial realm of Stromgarde. For ages, Stromgarde stood as a bastion of stalwart warriors dedicated to keeping the forest trolls at bay.",sp=0},{t="A Shattered Kingdom",b="Stromgarde proved vital in defending the Alliance during the Second War under King Thoras Trollbane, but the Third War and its aftermath shattered the nation. Although the kingdom spared itself the worst ravages of the Scourge plague, the mysterious death of King Thoras threw the realm into turmoil. Boulderfist ogres swept in from the hills, while the traitorous Alteraci nobles of the Syndicate seized sprawling districts of Stromgarde Keep. Today, Prince Galen Trollbane and his loyalist survivors cling to a tiny sliver of the city and their redoubt at Refuge Pointe, waging a bitter guerrilla war against hopeless odds.",sp=0},{t="The War for the Highlands",b="Arathi is a fiercely contested crossroads. In the northeast, the Horde converted an abandoned human internment camp into Hammerfall, named in honor of the legendary Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, using it as an anchor to secure their northern holdings and safeguard allies in Hillsbrad. Meanwhile, the Witherbark troll tribe seeks vengeance against their ancient human persecutors, and the Argus Wake pulls strings behind the Syndicate's occupation. At the center of the plateau lie ancient Circles of Binding, where bound elementals restrain an enigmatic, ancient power buried beneath the stone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Stromgarde Keep?",a="Following King Thoras Trollbane's death, Stromgarde succumbed to internal strife and overwhelming assaults. Boulderfist ogres seized the city's exterior districts while the opportunistic Syndicate seized the sanctum, leaving Prince Galen Trollbane and his dwindling garrison clinging to a single fortified corner while fighting desperate battles inside their own capital.",al={"why is stromgarde ruined","who controls stromgarde","stromgarde status"}},{q="What is Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is a fortified Horde outpost built within the remnants of a human internment camp where orcs were held after the Second War. It was named to honor former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell leading the campaign to liberate the captives held across Lordaeron's camps.",al={"horde base arathi","history of hammerfall","why is it called hammerfall"}},{q="Where does the Alliance operate in Arathi?",a="Alliance soldiers and Stromgarde defenders stage their operations out of Refuge Pointe, a naturally fortified canyon in the center of the highlands. From here, they launch sorties to reclaim Stromgarde Keep and fight back encroaching ogres and trolls.",al={"alliance base arathi","refuge pointe","where are the stromgarde humans"}},{q="What are the stone circles across the plains?",a="The Circles of Binding—Inner, Outer, East, and West—are ancient magical seals maintained and guarded by rogue elementals. They serve to imprison an unknown, primordial entity buried deep beneath the highlands.",al={"circles of binding","elementals in arathi","stone circles"}},{q="How do you reach the Arathi Highlands?",a="Travelers from the north and west pass through the breach in Thoradin's Wall from the Hillsbrad Foothills. Travelers arriving from Khaz Modan in the south cross the massive dwarven bridge of the Thandol Span, which spans the chasm separating the highlands from the Wetlands.",al={"getting to arathi","how to get to arathi highlands","arathi entrance"}},{q="What is the Syndicate doing in Arathi?",a="The Syndicate consists of exiled Alteraci nobility seeking to carve out new domains by pillaging fallen realms. In Arathi, they have overrun large sections of Stromgarde Keep and outlying farms like Northfold Manor.",al={"why is syndicate in arathi","syndicate stromgarde","who leads the syndicate here"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Human"]="Every human kingdom traces its roots to the Empire of Arathor; seeing the seat of human civilization broken and overrun by ogres and thieves is a profound cultural tragedy.",["faction:Horde"]="Hammerfall stands as sacred ground to the modern Horde—a monument to Orgrim Doomhammer's sacrifice that freed an enslaved people from internment.",["class:Warrior"]="Stromgarde produced the most celebrated frontline martial tradition on Azeroth, making its rugged battlegrounds a revered trial by arms.",["profession:Mining"]="The craggy ridges of Arathi are rich in iron and mithril, and Drywhisker Gorge is the only known source of lesser bloodstone ore."},kw={"arathi","arathi highlands","arathor","boulderfist","galen trollbane","hammerfall","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","thandol span","thoradin's wall"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:thoradin-s-wall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:hillsbrad","zone:wetlands"},src={"Arathi Highlands (Classic)","Arathi Highlands"}}
